'''Billy''' is a [[mountain goat]] who is found within the fencing of [[Tenzing]]'s house.

A second Billy was discovered in the [[Great Kourend|Kingdom of Great Kourend]], located on a small island in the north-eastern corner of Great Kourend's [[Port Piscarilius]].

==Lore==
In spite of what initial appearances may suggest, the seemingly marooned mountain goat north of Port Piscarilius is canonically considered not to be stuck on the islet, but rather to sojourn there out of his own free volition.{{CiteTwitter|author=Mod Ash|url=https://twitter.com/JagexAsh/status/1677674136888389632|date=8 July 2023|archiveurl=https://reldo.runescape.wiki/i/97506|archivedate=9 July 2023|quote=[just wondering is there any story as to why Billy the goat is stuck on an island north of port pisc?] (...) Goats are broadly able to leap and scale cliffs, so the character is not considered in lore to be stuck; he could leave if he wished, though he so far does not wish to.}} The solitary animal is also capable of finding enough sustenance on the islet to survive, even though no vegetation appears to subsist on the skerry.{{CiteTwitter|author=Mod Ash|url=https://twitter.com/JagexAsh/status/1472946753850720263|date=20 December 2021|archiveurl=https://reldo.runescape.wiki/i/99582|archivedate=12 July 2023|quote=[Sir! we have to save this goat he is all alone he cant survive there!!!!! [https://reldo.runescape.wiki/i/100839]] He clearly can!}}

Billy is said to have leapt onto the islet from the coastal bluffs stretched along Kourend's north-eastern shoreline, the watershed dividing the [[Western Ocean]] from the valley carved out by the [[River of Souls]].{{CiteTwitter|author=Mod Ash|url=https://twitter.com/JagexAsh/status/1368181329502871554|date=6 March 2021|archiveurl=https://reldo.runescape.wiki/i/102193|archivedate=11 July 2023|quote=[Living my best life on #OSRS digging up sandworms and notice poor old Billy 🐐 stranded on a small island 🏝 off the coast of Piscarilius. @JagexAsh how did he get out there! Can we have a new quest to rescue him? #SaveBilly] He'd have jumped across from the adjacent cliffs, I think. Goats are great at climbing and leaping, right? I'm sure he's fine.}} However, other interpretations of how the goat landed ashore can also be advanced: [[Odd Mushroom]] for instance had been known to combine certain salts in order to teleport goats.{{CiteText|text=Weiss fire notes|author=Odd Mushroom|quote=With the correct combination of salts, the basalt can be made to transport matter - rocks, logs, even living creatures like goats - from place to place.}}

