{{External|rs=Bind (spell)}} {{Infobox Spell |name = Bind |image = [[File:Bind.png]] |release = [[29 March]] [[2004]] |update = RS2 Launched! |members = No |level = 20 |spellbook = Normal |type = Combat |exp = 31 |damage = 0 |cost = {{RuneReq|Nature=2|Earth=3|Water=3}} |speed = 5 ticks |description = Holds your opponent for 5 seconds |anim = [[File:Bind.gif|300px]] |sound = [[File:Bind.ogg]] }} [[File:Bind icon (mobile).png|left]] '''Bind''' is a level 20 [[Magic]] [[Spells|spell]] located in the [[Standard spellbook]]. Casting bind on an opponent will prevent it from moving for 8 [[ticks]] (4.8 seconds). When used on a player and the bind is about to wear off, the bound player will receive this message in their chatbox: {{mes|The holding effect is beginning to fade.|color=red}} Players can increase the binding duration by equipping [[swampbark armour]]; the [[Swampbark helm|helm]], [[Swampbark body|body]], and [[Swampbark legs|legs]] will increase the duration by 2 [[ticks]] (1.2 seconds) each, up to a maximum of 14 [[ticks]] (8.4 seconds).
Bind gives 31 Magic [[experience]] if it successfully hits the target, or 30 experience if it [[splash]]es. It requires two [[Nature rune|nature]], three [[Earth rune|earth]], and three [[water rune]]s to be cast.
==Cost== {{Spell cost table |Rune1 = Water |Rune1num = 3 |Rune2 = Earth |Rune2num = 3 |Rune3 = Nature |Rune3num = 2 |uses_pages_water = yes }} {| class="wikitable" |+ ! colspan="3" |Wilderness-only casting |- |{{CostLine|Blighted entangle sack}} |}
==Changes== {{Subject changes header}} {{Subject changes |date = 13 September 2023 |update = The Path of Glouphrie |change = Bind now yields 31 [[Magic]] [[experience]] upon a successful cast. }} {{Subject changes |date = 21 June 2023 |update = More Poll 79 Changes |poll = Old School Content Poll 79: Quality of Life |change = * The maximum Swampbark Armour set bonus for the Bind spell can now be achieved with just the [[Swampbark helm|helm]], [[Swampbark_body|body]] and [[Swampbark_legs|legs]] as opposed to the full set. * Each outfit piece now increases the duration of the Bind spell by an additional [[tick]], so the complete bonus increases the duration to 6 ticks. }} {{Subject changes |date = 11 January 2023 |update = Secrets of the North & More! |change = An audio cue and message have been added to the Bind spell to tell the victims when the freeze is about to expire. }} {{Subject changes |date = 5 September 2019 |update = PvP Balancing, LMS, and Elf Graphics |change = [[Protect from Magic]] no longer halves the duration of Bind. }} {{Subject changes footer}}
{{Standard spellbook}}

{{External|rs}} {{Infobox Item |name = Binding fluid |image = [[File:Binding fluid.png]] |release = [[19 February]] [[2007]] |update = The Tower of Life |members = Yes |quest = [[Tower of Life]] |tradeable = No |equipable = No |stackable = No |noteable = No |options = Drop |examine = Some magical fluid to bind surfaces. |value = 1 |weight = 0.010 |id = 10870 }} [[File:Binding fluid detail.png|left|130px]] '''Binding fluid''' is an item found during the [[Tower of Life]] [[quest]]. It is found in a crate inside the tower on the south side.
A player must use 5 [[metal bar]]s and 4 bottles of binding fluid to repair the [[cage (Tower of Life)#Unfixed|broken cage]] on the {{FloorNumber|uk=3}} floor of the [[Tower of Life (building)|tower]]. Additional bottles of binding fluid can be obtained before the broken cage is fixed, and fixing the broken cage will only remove 4 bottles of binding fluid.
{{Tower of Life}}

{{External|rs}} {{Infobox Item |name = Binding necklace |image = [[File:Binding necklace.png]] |release = [[13 June]] [[2005]] |update = RuneCraft Update and Tweaks |members = Yes |quest = No |tradeable = Yes |equipable = Yes |stackable = No |noteable = Yes |options = Wear, Check, Destroy |wornoptions = Check |destroy = This will destroy your necklace along with any charges on it. Are you sure? |examine = A necklace embedded with mystical power. |value = 1425 |weight = 0.010 |exchange = Yes |id = 5521 }} [[File:Binding necklace detail.png|left|130px]] The '''binding necklace''' is an [[enchanted jewellery|enchanted]] [[emerald necklace]] that gives the wearer a 100% success rate in making [[combination rune]]s through the [[Runecraft]] skill. It has 16 uses (one use is one click on an altar) and will be destroyed once all are used. It has a right-click "check" option that shows how many charges are left.
Similar to a [[ring of recoil]], binding necklace charges are stored per player, not per necklace. Thus if the player sells or casts High Level Alchemy on a necklace with 1 charge remaining, the next necklace the player equips will still have only 1 charge. The player can right-click to "destroy" a binding necklace, destroying it and restoring the next binding necklace the player equips to 16 charges. This can be useful when a necklace drops to 1 charge left and a player is crafting runes in pairs, where a player can destroy a second necklace in their inventory and the equipped one will regain charges.
Players with 27 Magic or higher can make it by casting [[Lvl-2 Enchant]] on an [[Emerald necklace]]. It can also be obtained as a drop by the [[Abyssal monsters|monsters in the Abyss]].
Prior to [[Update:Colourful Golems & Graphical Improvements|an update]], the binding necklace was one of only two pieces of jewellery to change their appearance slightly upon being enchanted, the other being the [[amulet of fury]].
