{{External|rs=Birdhouse}} {{Otheruses|def=no|bird houses in general|Bird house trapping|the placed down trap|Birdhouse (scenery)}} {{Infobox Item |name = Bird house |image = [[File:Bird house.png]] |release = [[7 September]] [[2017]] |update = Fossil Island |members = Yes |quest = No |tradeable = Yes |equipable = No |stackable = No |noteable = Yes |options = Drop |examine = Feed and catch the birds by placing this in the right spot. |value = 5 |weight = 0.453 |exchange = Yes |id = 21512 }} [[File:Bird house detail.png|left|130x200px]] A '''bird house''' is used to set [[bird house traps]] on [[Fossil Island]] requiring 5 [[Hunter]]. It can be made at 5 [[Crafting]] using [[logs]] on a [[clockwork]] with a [[chisel]] and [[hammer]] yielding 15 [[experience]].
Once placed in a [[bird house space]], it becomes a [[Birdhouse (scenery)|birdhouse trap]].
Bird houses must be baited with 10 [[hop seed]]s (5 if [[wildblood seed|Wildblood]]), 10 [[allotment seed]]s, 10 [[flower seed]]s, 10 low level [[herb seeds]] ([[Guam seed|guam]], [[Marrentill seed|marrentill]], [[Tarromin seed|tarromin]], [[Harralander seed|harralander]]), or 5 high level herb seeds ([[Rannar seed|ranarr]] and above). After approximately 50 minutes when the birdhouse is full, it can be emptied, granting 280 [[Hunter]] experience.
==Creation== {{Recipe |skill1 = Crafting |skill1lvl = 5 |skill1boostable = Yes |skill1exp = 15 |members = Yes |ticks = 2 |ticksnote = Make-all is 2, then 3 ticks. |tools = Chisel, Hammer |mat1 = Logs |mat2 = Clockwork |output1 = Bird house }}
{{Bird houses}}

{{External|rs=Birdhouses}}
[[File:Bird house trapping.png|thumb|300px|A bird house trap that has been set.]]
'''Bird house trapping''' is a [[Hunter]] technique that is used to catch birds. With this technique the player sets up bird houses on [[Fossil Island]] and fills them with seeds. The player then has to wait around 50 minutes for the bird houses to passively fill with birds.

==Bird houses==
Bird house traps are made using the [[Crafting]] skill requiring [[Woodcutting#Types_of_trees|logs]] and a piece of [[clockwork]] with a [[hammer]] and [[chisel]]. They are then placed in designated spots on [[Fossil Island]] to catch birds, providing a passive method of training Hunter and gaining resources.

Additionally, [[Ironman Mode|ironmen]] will need a [[Construction]] level of 25 to build a [[crafting table 2]] for assembling [[clockwork]].

{{/Table}}

==Seeds==
To arm the trap, players need 10 low level or 5 high level [[hop seed]]s, [[herb seeds]], [[flower seeds]], [[bush seeds]], or [[allotment seeds]]. By using less seeds than the required amount, different types of seeds can be used to set up the same trap (for example, it's possible to use a stack of 7 Barley seeds and fill the remaining 3 with Hammerstone).

All seeds give the exact same rewards, so it is recommended to use the seeds that are cheapest or easiest to obtain.{{CiteTwitter|author=Mod Ash|url=https://twitter.com/JagexAsh/status/1019209471015387138|date=17 July 2018|archiveurl=https://reldo.runescape.wiki/i/105153|archivedate=27 May 2020|quote=[Do the seeds you place in birdhouses have an effect on the amount of nests you get?] No.|name=ashseedstweet}}

Low-level ironmen can buy a wide variety of seeds from [[Draynor Seed Market]] or [[Amelia's Seed Shop]] in the farming guild at a relative low price. The 135 seeds in stock can be bought for 377 gp. Nevertheless, ironmen should consider hopping worlds as the number of seeds in stock varies between 5 and 20 per world (with a restock time of 1 minute). Ironmen may also find [[pickpocketing]] a [[Master Farmer]] to be a great source of surplus low level seeds. 

{{/Seeds}}

==Locations==
{{Map|width=300|height=300|3677,3882|3678,3815|3763,3755|3768,3761|align=right|mtype=pin}}
There are four spots on [[Fossil Island]] on which players can place bird house traps, indicated by the [[File:Bird house site icon.png]] icon.
*The first and second are found in the [[Verdant Valley]], south of the [[Museum Camp]].
*The third is found west of the [[ancient shroom]] in the [[Mushroom Forest]], and directly north of the [[Magic Mushtree|magic mushtree]].
*The fourth is found by the entrance to the [[Tar Swamp]].

All of these spots are easily accessible by using the [[Digsite pendant]] teleport to Fossil Island after using the pendant on the strange machine at the [[House on the Hill]], then using the [[magic mushtree]] in the House on the Hill.

==Catching birds==
After the bird house trap has been set and filled with seeds, it will passively capture birds at random intervals (an average of once every 5 minutes), up to a maximum of 10. To claim the Hunter experience and loot, players must return to the bird house trap to empty and dismantle it. The bird house will be lost in the process, but the clockwork will be returned, meaning players only need four clockworks to set all their bird houses indefinitely, after which they will only need to bring a hammer, chisel, logs, and seeds. However, it is recommended to bring an additional clockwork, as building the next bird house between the sites speeds up the process. 

When ready to harvest, bird houses have a reset option, which will empty the bird house and place a new bird house with a delay of one tick more than doing the process manually. If players wish to not bring an extra clockwork to pre-make bird houses, this process will also automatically construct a bird house and place it, though this is also slower than doing so manually. If the player has multiple types of logs in their inventory, there will still be a prompt for the type of log to use. This automated reset process also still requires adding the seeds manually.

===Recommended setup===
<div style="display:flex;justify-content:center;">
{{Inventory|Asgarnian seed\40|Clockwork|Hammer|Chisel|Redwood logs|Redwood logs|Redwood logs|Redwood logs|Digsite pendant|||||||||||||||||||
}}
{{Equipment
|neck = Strung rabbit foot
}}
</div>

The fastest route is to first teleport with the [[digsite pendant]] to [[Fossil Island]] and use the [[magic mushtree]] to [[Verdant Valley]]. The northern birdhouse should be checked first, then the southern. Next, teleport with the mushtree to [[Mushroom Meadow]] and check the birdhouse to the north, then run south to the Tar Swamp to check the final birdhouse.

Bringing an extra birdhouse or [[clockwork]] allows for the birdhouses to be crafted while running to the next location, saving a significant amount of time. The [[Imcando hammer]] may be brought in place of a hammer to save an inventory slot. A [[hunter potion]] or a [[super hunter potion]] may be brought to boost Hunter by +3 or +6 respectively to increase the odds of receiving bird nests or gain the level necessary to place the next tier of birdhouse.

If doing multiple birdhouse runs in a row, the player can log out while standing near the Tar Swamp birdhouse, in order to avoid the relatively long run south on the second run. The player would have to bring 4 extra logs to make this work.

Players may also wish to bring a [[Pestle and mortar]] in their inventory to crush the [[Bird nest (empty)|bird nests]] as they receive them. Doing this while running between birdhouse spots can save the player time when making [[Saradomin brew|saradomin brews]] by hand, or save the player a trip to [[Nardah]] to have [[Wesley]] crush them for 50gp each.

==Loot==
Once a birdhouse is full, it can be collected for loot, which includes [[raw bird meat]], [[feather]]s, and the [[clockwork]] that was used to build the birdhouse.

Birdhouses will also give varying numbers of [[bird nest]]s, dependent on the tier of birdhouse and [[Hunter]] level.{{CiteNews|author=The Old School Team|url=https://secure.runescape.com/m=news/bird-nest-balancing-and-pvp-changes?oldschool=1|title=Bird Nest Balancing and PvP Changes|newsdate=22 November 2018|name=BirdNestBalancing}} Each birdhouse will give at most 1 seed nest, followed by 10 chances to get nests off the nest table. The nest table drops regular [[Bird nest (empty)|empty nests]], [[Bird nest (ring)|ring nests]], [[Bird nest (egg)|egg nests]], and rarely also [[clue nest]]s (replaced with [[scroll box]]es if [[X Marks the Spot]] is completed).

In addition, wearing a [[strung rabbit foot]] will replace about 5% of the empty nest drops with ring nests or egg nests.{{CiteNews|author=The Old School Team|url=https://secure.runescape.com/m=news/collection-log-improvements-and-the-last-of-poll-74?oldschool=1|title=Collection Log Improvements and The Last of Poll 74|newsdate=7 April 2021}} This is different from the bird nest mechanic while [[Woodcutting]], which reduces the number of seed nests.

The seeds used do '''not''' affect amount of nests received.{{NamedRef|ashseedstweet}} Dismantling a birdhouse does not have a Hunter level requirement, meaning boosts only need to be used when placing higher tier birdhouses and not when dismantling them.

The birdhouse must be completely depleted of seeds before any rewards can be claimed from it. Emptying the birdhouse early (before the approximate 50 minutes) will save the clockwork but lose the birdhouse, the remaining seeds, and any loot that might have accumulated. A warning message is given in case the player selects the option to empty before the birdhouse is full. The time remaining can be roughly determined by checking the seed level in the birdhouse.

