A '''bird nest''' with a ring can be found while woodcutting most types of [[tree]]s, as well as several other activities. Bird nests contain a random [[gold ring|gold]], [[sapphire ring|sapphire]], [[emerald ring|emerald]], [[ruby ring|ruby]], or [[diamond ring]], and also provide an [[empty nest]]. The chance of getting a bird nest from a tree is 1/256 each time you would normally get a log, regardless of the type of tree. If a nest appears while a player is cutting a tree, a chirping sound will usually be heard, and the player will get a message in the chat box stating, "''{{Colour|#ff0000|A bird's nest falls out of the tree.}}''" The nest is dropped on the ground and will despawn after 2 minutes if not picked up. [[Redwood|Redwood trees]] do not drop ring nests, and instead only drop [[clue nest]]s.

When [[woodcutting]], a roll is done to determine the type of nest the player will receive. The table contains 100 slots: 3/100 [[Bird nest (egg)|egg nest]] (one for each colour), 32/100 ring nest, 65/100 [[Bird nest (seeds)|seed nest]]. When wearing a [[strung rabbit foot]], five seed slots are removed, making the chances 3/95 for bird's egg, 32/95 for ring and 60/95 for seeds.{{CiteTwitter|author=Mod Ash|url=https://twitter.com/JagexAsh/status/1055815273763217414|date=26 October 2018|archiveurl=https://reldo.runescape.wiki/i/102252|archivedate=26 May 2020|quote=If you've got the rabbit foot necklace, pick number 0-94 inclusive. Otherwise, pick number 0-99 inclusive. 0 = red egg, 1 = blue egg, 2 = green egg, 3-34 = ring, otherwise it's seeds.}}

During [[bird house trapping]], up to 10 nest rolls are performed with a chance of getting a ring nest. For successful rolls, the chance is 32/100 for a ring nest. Wearing a strung rabbit foot removes 5 empty nest slots, making the chance for a ring nest 32/95.

[[Wyson]] will sometimes reward ring nests in exchange for [[mole skin]]s and [[mole claw]]s, which will be packed in a [[nest box]] if there isn't enough room in the inventory to hold all the nests.

Ring nests are also rewarded from [[Managing Miscellania]] when subjects are tasked with collecting maple, teak or mahogany logs.

