{{External|rs}} {{Infobox Item |name = Bird snare |image = [[File:Bird snare.png]] |release = [[21 November]] [[2006]] |update = HUNTER SKILL! |members = Yes |quest = No |tradeable = Yes |equipable = No |stackable = Yes |noteable = No |options = Lay, Drop |examine = A simple bird catcher. |value = 5 |weight = 0.000 |respawn = 100 |exchange = Yes |id = 10006 }} [[File:Bird snare detail.png|left|130px]] A '''bird snare''' is a type of trap used in the [[Hunter]] skill. The bird snaring technique is used to catch several [[bird (disambiguation)|bird]]s. With the required Hunter level, the player may set up a bird snare and wait for a bird to approach the trap.
If the prey is successfully caught, the snare will trap the bird, and the player will have the option to "check" the trap. If not successful, the trap will still snap, and the player will have to reset it. A bird snare will not catch birds if the user is standing directly on the bird snare.
[[Hunter#Bait and smoking traps|Smoking]] a trap will increase the catch rate by +2%.{{CiteTwitter|author=Mod Ash|url=https://twitter.com/JagexAsh/status/793829284288851968|date=2 November 2016|archiveurl=https://reldo.runescape.wiki/i/105762|archivedate=15 August 2019|quote=+2% for the smoke, +3% for the bait.}} Due to the low increase of the catch rate, most players believe that smoking traps doesn't justify the extra actions it takes.
Bird snares may be bought from [[Aleck's Hunter Emporium.|Aleck's Hunter Emporium]] in [[Yanille]], the [[Nardah Hunter Shop]] in [[Nardah]], or [[Imia's Supplies]] in the [[Hunter Guild]]. One can also be obtained for free by searching the south-western [[crate (Land's End)|crate]] in [[Hugor]]'s house at [[Land's End]] (multiple snares can be obtained by dropping the snare and searching again).
Bird snares are also obtainable from a [[Hunter kit]], the only way native to the Fremennik region to acquire one and necessary to complete the [[Fremennik Diary]].
==Creatures== The following [[Hunter creatures]] may be caught using the bird snaring technique.
{| class="wikitable sortable align-center-1 align-center-2 align-center-4" !{{SCP|Hunter}} ! colspan=2 |Creature !Exp. !Location |- |1 ||{{plinkp|Crimson swift|pic=Crimson swift icon}} || [[Crimson swift]] ||34 ||[[Feldip Hunter area]], [[Tlati Rainforest]], [[Isle of Souls]], and [[Kebos Swamp]] |- |5 ||{{plinkp|Golden warbler|pic=Golden warbler icon}} || [[Golden warbler]] ||47 ||[[Uzer Hunter area]] |- |9 ||{{plinkp|Copper longtail|pic=Copper longtail icon}} || [[Copper longtail]] ||61 ||[[Piscatoris Hunter area]], [[Isle of Souls]], [[Kourend Woodland]], and [[Aldarin]] |- |11 ||{{plinkp|Cerulean twitch|pic=Cerulean twitch icon}} || [[Cerulean twitch]] ||64.6 ||[[Rellekka Hunter area]] and [[Mons Gratia]] |- |19 ||{{plinkp|Tropical wagtail|pic=Tropical wagtail icon}} || [[Tropical wagtail]] ||95 ||[[Feldip Hunter area]] and [[Tlati Rainforest]] |}
