{{External|rs}} {{Infobox Item |name = Bitternut |image = [[File:Bitternut.png]] |release = [[4 July]] [[2006]] |update = Trouble Brewing |members = Yes |quest = No |tradeable = No |bankable = No |equipable = No |stackable = No |noteable = No |options = Drop |examine = Monkeys seem to like throwing these. |value = 1 |weight = 0.003 |id = 8976 }} [[File:Bitternut detail.png|left|100px]] '''Bitternuts''' are items used in the [[Trouble Brewing]] minigame. Players can obtain the nuts from the bitternut trees found within the minigame on [[Mos Le'Harmless]] using [[Monkey (Trouble Brewing)|monkeys]], which are caught in the same area.
In order to retrieve a bitternut, the player must first dye a monkey in the colour of their team using [[Bowl of red water|red water]] or [[Bowl of blue water|blue water]], obtained by using either [[Red flowers (Trouble Brewing)|red]] or [[Blue flowers (Trouble Brewing)|blue flowers]] on the kettle in your team's base and then using an empty bowl on the kettle. They then can use the [[Monkey (Trouble Brewing)|monkey]] with the [[Bitternut Tree]].
Additionally, if you have a [[Monkeyspeak amulet]] or have completed [[Monkey Madness II]], you can alter the strategy used. You can choose to either make the monkey angry by taunting it, or caution him. By making him angry, he'll be more inclined to get up the tree as fast as possible and start pelting you with bitternuts, speeding up the time before you get a nut. If you tell him to be careful, he'll take a little bit longer, but will be more aware of other monkeys and will be more likely to win in a confrontation. This is also the most complicated task in [[Trouble Brewing]].
Players may only have 2 bitternuts in their inventory at one time. If the player attempts to gather more while having two in their inventory already, the monkey will return home without giving the player another bitternut. When obtained players are granted 50 [[Hunter]] experience. Bitternuts can be used on the team's hopper, gaining 200 [[Cooking]] experience in the process.
According to [[Varrock Museum]], monkeys on both [[Karamja]] and [[Mos Le'Harmless]] are very fond of bitternuts, although the nuts can only be found by players on [[Mos Le'Harmless]].
==Skill info== {{Skill info |version1 = Obtaining |version2 = Depositing |skill1name1 = Hunter |skill1name2 = Cooking |skill1lvl = 1 |skill1exp1 = 50 |skill1exp2 = 200 |item1 = [[Blue monkey]] or [[Red monkey]] |item2 = None |facility1 = [[Bitternut Tree]] |facility2 = [[Hopper (Trouble Brewing)]] }}
==Bitternut ballistics== A monkey cannot hit a brewer with a bitternut if they are further than 8 tiles removed from the bitternut tree, forming a 17x17 square pelting area centered on the tree's south-western tile.{{CiteTwitter|author=Mod Ash|url=https://twitter.com/JagexAsh/status/1172097743877279744|date=12 September 2019|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20190928025904/https://twitter.com/JagexAsh/status/1172097743877279744|archivedate=28 September 2019|quote=Are you 9+ tiles away from the tree when it fails to do this? It's checking to see if you're "too far away". (...)}} {{Map|x=3808|y=2974|width=600|height=200|zoom=3|align=left |mtype:polygon,3814:2964,3797:2964,3797:2981,3814:2981 |mtype:polygon,3791:2964,3774:2964,3774:2981,3791:2981 |mtype:polygon,3842:2967,3825:2967,3825:2984,3842:2984 }}{{Clear|left}}
