{{Otheruses|the [[Nightmare Zone]] variant|the quest boss fought during [[Holy Grail]]|Black Knight Titan}} {{Infobox Monster |version1 = Normal Mode |version2 = Hard Mode |name1 = Black Knight Titan |name2 = Black Knight Titan (hard) |image = [[File:Black Knight Titan (Nightmare Zone).png|180px]] |release = [[5 September]] [[2013]] |update = Will you wake up from the Nightmare Zone? |members = Yes |combat1 = 120 |combat2 = 210 |size = 1 |examine = He looks mean and powerful. |xpbonus1 = 2.5 |xpbonus2 = 5 |max hit1 = 15 |max hit2 = 28 |aggressive = Yes |poisonous = No |attack style = [[Crush]] |attack speed = 7 |hitpoints1 = 142 |hitpoints2 = 255 |att1 = 91 |att2 = 182 |str1 = 100 |str2 = 200 |def = 91 |mage = 1 |range = 1 |attbns = 27 |strbns = 22 |amagic = 0 |mbns = 0 |arange = 0 |rngbns = 0 |dstab = 18 |dslash = 27 |dcrush = 18 |dmagic = 1000 |dlight = 1000 |dstandard = 1000 |dheavy = 1000 |poisonresistance = 0 |venomresistance = 0 |id1 = 6360 |id2 = 6299 }} The '''Black Knight Titan''' is a boss that can be encountered in the [[Nightmare Zone]]. He is a version of the regular [[Black Knight Titan]] encountered in the [[Holy Grail]] quest. Like his normal counterpart, his attacks are slow and inaccurate, but he should be fought with Melee, as he has incredibly high Ranged and Magic defence.
[[Excalibur]] is not required to defeat him in the Nightmare Zone. Unlike the version fought in Holy Grail, you get full experience for damage dealt to him.
In Endurance mode, 2,934 reward points are earned upon defeating the normal difficulty version, and 10,127 reward points are earned upon defeating the hard difficulty version.
