[[File:Black dragon icon.png|left]]
'''Black dragons''' are the most powerful adult [[chromatic dragons|chromatic]] [[dragons]]. As with all adult dragons, protection from [[dragonfire]] (such as an [[anti-dragon shield]]) is recommended when fighting them, although like other common chromatic dragons, they only use dragonfire at melee range. 

Black dragons are the only common chromatic dragons that drop the [[draconic visage]]. Notably, the stronger level 247 variant in the [[Wilderness Slayer Cave]] drops the draconic visage at a rate of 1/5,000, the most common out of any dragon tied with the [[King Black Dragon]] and [[Vorkath]].

[[Baby black dragon]]s, [[brutal black dragon]]s, and the [[King Black Dragon]] may be killed in place of black dragons for a [[Slayer task]]; however, the KBD does '''not''' count towards a black dragon task assigned by [[Krystilia]]. Likewise, [[lava dragon]]s '''do not''' count towards a black dragon task, despite their [[black dragonhide]] drop.

One is fought during [[Dragon Slayer II]] and the [[Recipe for Disaster]] [[Recipe for Disaster/Freeing Sir Amik Varze|Sir Amik Varze subquest]].

