==Location comparisons==
In the [[Taverley Dungeon]], 2 black dragons spawn north-west near the [[Obelisk of Fire]] and can be safe-spotted behind the ladder, while 12 spawn in the upper level along with 5 baby black dragons. The ones in the upper level can only be killed when assigned black dragons as a Slayer task, otherwise the player will be stopped by [[Slieve]] if they attempt to attack them off-task. A [[dusty key]] or 70 [[Agility]] (80 if using the [[Strange floor (Taverley Dungeon)|strange floor]] shortcut) is required to access the west side of the dungeon; the task-only area can be accessed by using the steps near the entrance.

The [[Evil Chicken's Lair]] contains 4 black dragons. Killing them here requires starting [[Recipe for Disaster/Freeing Sir Amik Varze|Sir Amik Varze's subquest]] in [[Recipe for Disaster]], and until the [[dragon token]] is redeemed, they will only drop it and these are 100% drops. Accessing this area requires a [[raw chicken]] offered to the [[chicken shrine]] in [[Zanaris]]. The dragon token is no longer obtainable after completing the subquest.

The [[Corsair Cove Dungeon]] contains 2 black dragons. Accessing this area requires completion of [[Dragon Slayer II]], but it is the closest location to a bank.

In the [[Wilderness]], black dragons can be found in two locations: the [[Lava Maze Dungeon]] and [[Wilderness Slayer Cave]]. 2 spawn in the Lava Maze dungeon, although accessing them requires a lengthy trek through the maze unless the player has 82 Agility (boostable at 77). Some [[Poison#Curing_poison|antipoison]] may be needed due to the presence of [[poison spider]]s near the dragons. 3 also spawn in the Wilderness Slayer Cave; these are slightly stronger than the level 227 variant and reside in a [[multicombat area]], but are faster to access compared to the ones underneath the Lava Maze.

