{{Infobox Item |name = Black felling axe |image = [[File:Black felling axe.png]] |release = [[25 October]] [[2023]] |update = Forestry: Part Two |members = Yes |quest = No |tradeable = Yes |equipable = Yes |stackable = No |noteable = Yes |options = Wield, Drop |examine = A sinister looking felling axe. |value = 384 |weight = 1.814 |exchange = Yes |id = 28205 }} [[File:Black felling axe detail.png|left|150px]] The '''black felling axe''' is a type of [[felling axe]] requiring an [[Attack]] level of 10 to be equipped, and a [[Woodcutting]] level of 11 to be used. Players can create the axe by using a [[felling axe handle]] on a [[black axe]] while having a [[hammer]] in their inventory and standing next to an [[anvil]]; this process is '''irreversible''', but the felling axe itself remains tradeable.
Black felling axes will chop at the same speed as a normal black axe. If the player is carrying [[forester's ration]]s however (either in the inventory or inside a [[forestry kit]]), they will receive 10% more Woodcutting experience each time they successfully chop a tree and gain a 20% chance not to receive logs when chopping trees (or [[Tree roots (Forestry)|tree roots]] in the [[Forestry#Rising_Roots|Rising Roots]] forestry event), at the cost of consuming one ration. This also results in a 20% chance to not receive [[anima-infused bark]] from tree roots.
If the player has no rations on their person, the felling axe will function like a regular black axe.
==Combat stats== {{Infobox Bonuses |astab = -2 |aslash = +10 |acrush = +8 |amagic = 0 |arange = 0 |dstab = 0 |dslash = +1 |dcrush = 0 |dmagic = 0 |drange = 0 |str = +12 |rstr = 0 |mdmg = 0 |prayer = 0 |slot = 2h |speed = 7 |attackrange = 1 |combatstyle = Axe |image = [[File:Black felling axe equipped male.png|250px]] |altimage = [[File:Black felling axe equipped female.png|250px]] }}
{{CombatStyles|Axe|speed=7|attackrange=1}}
==Creation== {{Recipe |skill1 = Smithing |skill1lvl = 11 |skill1boostable = Yes |skill1exp = 5 |members = Yes |ticks = |tools = Hammer |facilities = Anvil |mat1 = Felling axe handle |mat2 = Black axe |output1 = Black felling axe }}
==Changes== {{Subject changes header}} {{Subject changes |date = 1 November 2023 |update = Forestry Tweaks, Security & More |change = A bug in which the XP bonus from felling axes did not correctly stack with the [[lumberjack outfit]] has been fixed. }} {{Subject changes |date = 25 October 2023 |update = Forestry: Part Two |change = * The item was made obtainable and [[members]]-only. * The item was renamed from "Black 2h axe" to "Black felling axe". * The item's weight was increased from 1.36 kg to 1.814 kg. * The item's [[value]] was increased from 161 to 384. * The item's examine was changed; previously, it was "''A woodcutter's axe.''" }} {{Subject changes |date = 28 June 2023 |update = Forestry: The Way of the Forester - Part One |change = The item was added to the game cache, but was unobtainable. }} {{Subject changes footer}}
{{Axe}} {{Black equipment}} {{Forestry}}

{{External|rs}} {{Infobox Item |name = Black flowers |image = [[File:Black flowers.png]] |release = [[29 March]] [[2004]] |update = RS2 Launched! |members = Yes |quest = No |tradeable = Yes |equipable = Yes |stackable = No |noteable = Yes |options = Wield, Drop |examine = A posy of flowers. |value = 100 |weight = 0.028 |exchange = Yes |id = 2476 }} [[File:Black flowers detail.png|left|130px]] '''Black flowers''' are a type of [[Flowers|flower]] that can be harvested after planting [[Mithril seeds|mithril]] or [[adamant seeds]]. Players have a 2/1,001 chance of obtaining a black flower when harvesting from a mithril or adamant seed.
When planting the seeds, players have an option to either pick the flowers (and obtaining a random coloured flower) or leave them planted on the ground. A player only has one chance to pick their flowers; if they refuse to do so, they '''will not''' get the option again unless they plant another seed. Flowers that are left on the ground will stay there temporarily for around 5 minutes.
Flowers can be wielded in the [[weapon slot]], and are classified as a [[fun weapon]] in legacy duels within the [[Emir's Arena]] because it gives the wielding player negative bonuses.
