{{External|rs}} {{otheruses|the equipable weapon|the [[Hunter]] creature|Black salamander (Hunter)}} {{Infobox Item |name = Black salamander |image = [[File:Black salamander.png]] |release = [[21 November]] [[2006]] |update = HUNTER SKILL! |members = Yes |quest = No |tradeable = Yes |equipable = Yes |stackable = No |noteable = Yes |options = Wield, Release |examine = Slightly slimy and somewhat menacing. |value = 200 |weight = 4.000 |exchange = Yes |id = 10148 }} [[File:Black salamander detail.png|left|130px]] [[File:Salamander attack.gif|frame|A player attacks using a salamander.]] The '''black salamander''' is the second strongest [[salamander]] that can be caught using the [[Hunter]] skill at level 67 Hunter, giving 319 experience per catch. They can be found north-east of the [[Chaos Temple (Wilderness)|Chaos Temple]].
It is a two-handed weapon that requires level 70 [[Attack]], [[Magic]], and [[Ranged]] to wield, and can be used to train [[Strength]], Magic, and Ranged. [[Harralander tar]] is used as ammunition for the salamander.
Despite being able to perform Magic and Ranged attacks, this weapon requires the user to be in the opponent's [[melee]] distance to attack, potentially reducing the practicality of the two attack styles. However, it can be used to attack enemies from behind fences, and can also attack enemies in diagonal squares, meaning that [[safespot]]ting is still possible.
When using the Scorch (Slash) and Blaze (Magic) attack styles, the attack speed is 5. When using the Flare (Range) attack style, the attack speed is 4, which is similar in concept to the Rapid style of most ranged weapons, and it will use standard{{CiteTwitter|author=Mod Ash|url=https://x.com/JagexAsh/status/1812764898239107397?t=0cPxrFVCvgFX01UUhSnWsg|date=15 July 2024|archiveurl=https://reldo.runescape.wiki/i/27963964|archivedate=2 May 2026|quote="standard"|notes=|name=|group=}} ranged defence, similar to [[bows]].
'''Warning:''' This is a live creature; if [[Protect Item|unprotected]] it will run away when you [[Death|die]]. Should this happen, you will need to buy or catch a new one.
==Combat stats== {{Infobox Bonuses |astab = 0 |aslash = +59 |acrush = 0 |amagic = 0 |arange = +69 |dstab = 0 |dslash = 0 |dcrush = 0 |dmagic = 0 |drange = 0 |str = +71 |rstr = 0 |mdmg = 0 |prayer = 0 |slot = 2h |speed = 5 |attackrange = 1 |combatstyle = Salamander |image = [[File:Black salamander equipped.png|120px]] |altimage = [[File:Black salamander equipped female.png|120px]] }}
{{CombatStyles|Salamander|speed=5|attackrange=1}}
==Chance to hit== Each attack style uses its own respective attack bonus (Slash, Range, Magic) when calculating a [[successful hit]]. Players looking to use two or more attack styles should take care in selecting equipment that does not penalize those attack bonuses.
==Experience== Due to the nature of salamanders, combat experience is rewarded normally. However you will get less magic experience per attack because there isn't a base experience amount per cast as with other spells. {| class="wikitable" |- style="font-weight:bold;" ! Combat Style ! Type ! Experience |- | Scorch | Slash | <math>StrengthExp = 4 \times Damage</math> |- | Flare | Ranged | <math>RangedExp = 4 \times Damage</math> |- | Blaze | Magic | <math>MagicExp = 2 \times Damage</math> |}
==Maximum hit== For melee mode the strength bonus of the salamander is used, which is 71 (same as a [[dragon longsword]]).
For ranged mode the ranged strength bonus of the tar is used to decide the maximum hit. The black salamander uses [[harralander tar]]s which have a ranged strength bonus of 49 (same as [[rune arrows]]).
The maximum hit for magic mode uses the "magic damage bonus" of the salamander. This bonus is not visible in the equipment stats, but is equal to 92 for the black salamander. Damage boosting items such as the [[slayer helmet (i)]] and [[occult necklace]] can be used to increase the max hit.
The max hit (Hit<sub>max</sub>) formula for salamanders is as shown in fig.1, where "Magic" is your visible magic level and "Bonus" is the "magic strength bonus" for the salamander, in this case 92. This gives us the formula for the black salamander as shown in fig.2.
<math>\begin{align} \text{Hit}_\text{max} &= \lfloor \frac{1}{2} + \frac{\text{Magic} \times (64 + \text{Bonus})}{640} \rfloor && (1) \\ \text{Hit}_\text{max} &= \lfloor \frac{1}{2} + \frac{\text{Magic} \times 156}{640} \rfloor && (2) \end{align}</math>
The table below shows maximum hits from level 70 to level 125. Like all other magic attacks, the max hit damage can be increased by using [[magic damage]] boosting equipment.
{| class="wikitable align-center-1 align-right-2" !{{SCP|Magic}} Level !Max Hit |- |70&ndash;71 |17 |- |72&ndash;75 |18 |- |76&ndash;79 |19 |- |80&ndash;84 |20 |- |85&ndash;88 |21 |- |89&ndash;92 |22 |- |93&ndash;96 |23 |- |97&ndash;100 |24 |- |101&ndash;104 |25 |- |105&ndash;108 |26 |- |109-112 |27 |- |113-116 |28 |- |117-121 |29 |- |122-125 |30 |}
