{{Infobox Item |name = Black tourmaline core |image = [[File:Black tourmaline core.png]] |release = [[26 October]] [[2017]] |update = Grotesque Guardians |members = Yes |quest = No |tradeable = Yes |equipable = No |stackable = No |noteable = Yes |options = Inspect, Drop |examine = The blackened heart of the Grotesque Guardians. |value = 41500 |weight = 1.000 |exchange = Yes |id = 21730 |leagueRegion = Morytania }} [[File:Black tourmaline core detail.png|left|150px]] The '''black tourmaline core''' is an item dropped by the [[Grotesque Guardians]] that can be found on the [[Slayer Tower]]'s rooftop. It can be used to upgrade the [[Bandos boots]] to create [[guardian boots]], after which the core is used up. This process is '''irreversible.'''
In the book [[The living statues]], it's revealed that the core was used by the [[Bandosian]] general [[Snaarldor]] to animate the statues of the Slayer Tower, giving life to the Grotesque Guardians as well as all the [[gargoyles]] in the tower. However, the gargoyles turned against the Bandosians after being ordered to attack [[Zamorakian]] forces. This was due to the Slayer Tower being filled with Zamorakian magic, as the creator of the tower, [[Viggora]], was a Zamorakian.
