{{External|rs}} {{Otheruses|def=no|other variants of the blade|Blade of saeldor (disambiguation)}} {{Infobox Item |defver = 2 |version1 = Inactive |version2 = Charged |name1 = Blade of saeldor (inactive) |name2 = Blade of saeldor |image1 = [[File:Blade of saeldor (inactive).png]] |image2 = [[File:Blade of saeldor.png]] |release = [[25 July]] [[2019]] |update = Song of the Elves |members = Yes |quest = No |tradeable1 = Yes |tradeable2 = No |equipable = Yes |stackable = No |noteable1 = Yes |noteable2 = No |options1 = Wield, Drop |options2 = Wield, Check, Uncharge, Drop |wornoptions = Check |examine = A magical elven sword. |value = 5000000 |weight = 1.814 |exchange1 = Yes |exchange2 = No |id1 = 23997 |id2 = 23995 |leagueRegion = Tirannwn }} {{Synced switch |version1=[[File:Blade of saeldor (inactive) detail.png|left|140px]] |version2=[[File:Blade of saeldor detail.png|left|140px]] }} The '''blade of Saeldor''' is a one-handed sword that once belonged to [[Saeldor]], an elite elven warrior, that can be created from an [[enhanced crystal weapon seed]]. Requiring level 80 [[Attack]] to wield, it provides the highest strength and slash bonus out of any weapon for its [[attack speed]], surpassing the [[abyssal tentacle]] as the best [[slash weapon]]. It is tied for the strongest one-handed melee weapon with the [[Ghrazi rapier]] and the [[Inquisitor's mace]], though these weapons are weaker than [[Osmumten's fang]] against high-defence monsters.
On unprotected death in [[Player killing|PvP]], the inactive blade is dropped, and all shards used to charge it will be lost. In [[PvM]] on the other hand, all current charges will be kept upon death.
