{{CombatStyles|Slash Sword|speed=4|attackrange=1}}
==Creation== Players can create the blade of Saeldor via a [[singing bowl]] by combining 100 [[crystal shard]]s and an [[enhanced crystal weapon seed]]. Doing so requires level 82 [[Smithing]] and [[Crafting]] to [[crystal singing|sing]] the crystal (the levels can be [[Temporary skill boost|boosted]]), and grants 5,000 experience in both skills. If the player does not meet the Smithing and Crafting requirements, they can have [[Conwenna]] or [[Reese]] sing the crystal for them for an extra 50 crystal shards, for a total of 150. {{#vardefine:crystalshardvalue|{{#ifexpr:{{#vardefineecho:seedvalue|{{GEP|Enhanced crystal teleport seed}} / 150}} > {{#vardefineecho:divinesupercombatvalue|({{GEP|Divine super combat potion(4)}} - {{GEP|Super combat potion(4)}}) / 0.4}} | {{#var:seedvalue}} | {{#var:divinesupercombatvalue}}}}}} {{Recipe |skill1 = Smithing |skill1lvl = 82 |skill1boostable = Yes |skill1exp = 5,000 |skill2 = Crafting |skill2lvl = 82 |skill2boostable = Yes |skill2exp = 5,000 |members = Yes |ticks = 5 |ticksnote = Takes 5 ticks to create an entire inventory |facilities = Singing bowl |mat1 = Enhanced crystal weapon seed |mat2 = Crystal shard |mat2quantity = 100 |mat2cost = {{#var:crystalshardvalue}} |mat2itemnote = Value based on {{#ifexpr:{{#var:seedvalue}} > {{#var:divinesupercombatvalue}} | the cost of obtaining by exchanging [[enhanced crystal teleport seed]]s with [[Amrod]] | the potential profit of using the crystal shards to create [[divine super combat potion]]s}} |output1 = Blade of saeldor |output1cost = {{GEP|Blade of saeldor (inactive)}} + {{#var:crystalshardvalue}} * (10000 / 100) |output1itemnote = Starts with 10,000 charges. Value is that of an inactive blade plus the cost of charging it. The tradeable inactive blade is worth {{Coins|{{GEP|Blade of saeldor (inactive)}}}}. }} {{Recipe |members = Yes |ticks = 0 |mat1 = Blade of saeldor (c) |mat1cost = {{GEP|Blade of saeldor (inactive)}} + {{#var:crystalshardvalue}} * (100000 / 100) |output1 = Blade of saeldor (inactive) |output1pic = Blade of saeldor (inactive) |output1cost = {{GEP|Blade of saeldor (inactive)}} }}
==Degradation== When created, the blade starts off at 10,000 charges and degrades like all [[crystal equipment]], with one charge being depleted for each hit, whether it is a successful one or not; once the blade's charges have been fully depleted, it will become inactive and lose its stat bonuses until more charges are added to it. Wearing an [[elven signet]] '''will not''' provide the chance to not consume charges.
In order to add charges to the blade, [[crystal shard]]s must be used on it (this can be done before it is inactive as well), with each shard granting 100 charges, up to a maximum of 20,000. Unlike other crystal equipment, players cannot directly revert the blade to an [[enhanced crystal weapon seed]]. In order to receive the seed back, players must bring an inactive blade to a [[singing bowl]] to revert it, costing 250 crystal shards. This is not recommended, as players can just sell the inactive blade on the [[Grand Exchange]].
Players can configure the charges while the weapon is in their bank by right-clicking on Configure-Charges, as long as players have the required materials.
Using the shard value of making [[divine super combat potion]]s, the cost per charge is {{Coins|({{GEP|Divine super combat potion(4)}}-{{GEP|Super combat potion(4)}})*0.025}}. Using the shard cost of trading in [[enhanced crystal teleport seed]]s to [[Amrod]], the most efficient option for buying crystal shards directly, the cost per charge is {{Coins|{{GEP|Enhanced_crystal_teleport_seed}}*0.00006666666}}. As a comparison, the [[abyssal tentacle]] costs {{Coins|{{GEP|Abyssal whip|0.0001}}}} per charge.
==Upgrading== The blade can be upgraded by [[Blade of saeldor (c)|corrupting]] it, which requires bringing the blade and 1,000 [[crystal shard]]s to a [[singing bowl]]. Doing so requires level 82 [[Smithing]] and [[Crafting]] (both levels can be [[Temporary skill boost|boosted]]), and grants no experience. If the player does not meet the Smithing and Crafting requirements, they can have [[Conwenna]] or [[Reese]] sing the crystal for them for an extra 500 crystal shards.
The corrupted blade stays charged permanently, and does not consume any [[Crystal shard|crystal shards]]. While the infinite version is untradeable, it can be reverted to an uncharged state at any time, but the shards used will be permanently lost in doing so.
Progress can also be made towards corruption through consuming charges with the blade, indicated through the "Check" option. Each 1% progress is equivalent to 1,000 charges used, which costs 10 crystal shards. Any combination of progress towards corruption, charges in the blade, and crystal shards can be used to meet the 1,000 crystal shard requirement to corrupt the blade. For example, a newly created blade will have 10,000 charges and only costs 900 crystal shards to corrupt.
If the blade reaches 100% progress towards corruption, it will still continue to consume charges until it is corrupted at the singing bowl, and the level 82 Smithing and Crafting requirements are still needed to avoid paying Conwenna or Reese an extra 500 crystal shards to corrupt it on the player's behalf.
If purchasing crystal seeds to [[Crystal shard#Exchanging_seeds|exchange into shards]], the cost for corrupting the blade is {{Coins|{{Min|{{GEP|Crystal weapon seed}}/10|{{GEP|Crystal tool seed}}/100|{{GEP|Enhanced crystal teleport seed}}/150|{{GEP|Crystal armour seed}}/250|{{GEP|Enhanced crystal weapon seed}}/1500}}*1000}}.
