{{Otheruses|def=no|other variants of the blade|Blade of saeldor (disambiguation)}} {{Infobox Item |name = Blade of saeldor (c) |image = [[File:Blade of saeldor (c).png]] |release = [[8 April]] [[2020]] |update = Poll 70 Improvements |members = Yes |quest = No |tradeable = No |equipable = Yes |stackable = No |noteable = No |options = Wield, Uncharge, Drop |examine = A magical elven sword, corrupted through the addition of too many shards. |value = 5000000 |weight = 1.814 |id = 24551 |leagueRegion = Tirannwn }} [[File:Blade of saeldor (c) detail.png|left|140px]] The '''blade of Saeldor (c)''' is a corrupted version of the [[blade of Saeldor]] that does not [[Degradation|degrade]], with its appearance altered to resemble the corrupted crystal seen within the [[Corrupted Gauntlet]]. The blade's colours may be changed to other colours of the [[Elven Clans]] by buying crystals from [[Lliann's Wares]] in [[Prifddinas]], which cost 500,000 coins each. It can also be reverted to its original colour by using the [[crystal of Hefin]] on any variant of the corrupted blade.
The blade can be upgraded by bringing it and 1,000 [[crystal shard]]s to a [[singing bowl]]. Doing so requires level 82 [[Smithing]] and [[Crafting]] (the levels can be [[Temporary skill boost|boosted]]), and grants no experience. If the player does not meet the Smithing and Crafting requirements, they can have [[Conwenna]] or [[Reese]] sing the crystal for them for an extra 500 crystal shards. Excess charges in the blade will be taken into account; for example, a fully charged blade (20,000 charges) will only cost 800 crystal shards to upgrade. Upon creating the corrupted blade, the chatbox message states "''With the help of the crystal bowl, you sing a dark song which corrupts the crystals.''"
While untradeable, the blade can be uncharged, but the crystal shards used to upgrade it will '''not''' be returned.
Like its regular variant, the blade requires level 80 [[Attack]] to wield, and provides the highest strength and slash bonus out of any weapon for its [[attack speed]], surpassing the [[abyssal tentacle]] as the best [[slash weapon]]. It is tied with the [[Ghrazi rapier]] as the second strongest one-handed melee weapon in the game, after the [[Inquisitor's mace]], although it is outperformed by the [[Scythe of Vitur]] against large monsters.
