{{disambig}}

{{Shelved content}}
The '''bladed moon''' was a scrapped [[Slash weapons|slash-focused]] shield slot item originally pitched as a reward for the [[Moons of Peril]] (then called Perilous Moons) in the [[Update:Perilous Moons - First Look & Rewards|Perilous Moons - First Look & Rewards]] update blog:

{{Infotable Bonuses header}}
{{Infotable Bonuses row|nolink=yes|hideicon=yes|name=Bladed moon|astab=+11|aslash=+59|acrush=0|amagic=-6|arange=-5|dstab=+7|dslash=+46|dcrush=+23|dmagic=-1|drange=+24|str=+5|rstr=0|mdmg=0|prayer=0}}
{{Infotable Bonuses footer}}

The bladed moon would have required level 65 [[Defence]] to wield, and would be an untradeable item created by combining spikes from the Blood, Blue, and Eclipse Moons.

Due to concerns about its stats as well as its potential to buff the then-dominant [[Osmumten's fang]] in slash mode, the item was iterated on a number of times in subsequent dev blogs and updates. 

A few days after the first look at the proposed rewards, the blog was updated to say that the bladed moon would only work with slash-based weapons, which would not include the stab-based Osmumten's fang (regardless of attack style). In the [[Update:Poll Blog: Fortis Colosseum x Perilous Moons|Fortis Colosseum x Perilous Moons Poll Blog]] a few days later, due to continued concerns about the item, it was decided not to include it as a polled reward, with plans to poll it at a later date.

During a later [[Update:Varlamore: Part One - Reward Changes|Varlamore Reward Changes Poll Blog]], the bladed moon was proposed again with one less strength bonus. One day later, due to community concerns about its damage when combined with strong slash weapons such as the [[Blade of Saeldor]], confusion about its place in item progression between the [[dragon defender]] and [[Avernic defender]], and a general lack of resonance with players, the bladed moon was again shelved and removed from the planned poll.

==Trivia==
* Despite not being in the game, the bladed moon is mentioned in the Defence level-up message for level 65.

{{Neypotzli}}

{{Infobox Weapon Group
|name = Bladed staff
|images = {{plinkp|Staff of the dead}} {{plinkp|Staff of light}} {{plinkp|Staff of balance}} {{plinkp|Toxic staff of the dead}} {{plinkp|Blue moon spear}}
|primary = [[Magic]]
|secondary = [[Melee]]
|speed = 4
}}
'''Bladed staves''' are a [[Weapons/Categories|category]] of [[magic]] [[weapons]] that typically possess both high [[melee]] and magic bonuses and can [[autocast]] spells.

Like [[spear]]s and [[hastae]], bladed staves have options for [[stab]], [[slash]], and [[crush]] attack styles. They can be thought of as spears/hastae that have the ability to autocast, much like how [[staves]] can be thought of as [[polestaff|polestaves]] that have the ability to autocast; however, bladed staves cannot be [[poisoned]].

Most bladed staves are one-handed weapons, have no crush bonus, have a melee [[attack speed]] of 4 - on par with the fastest melee weapons with attack bonuses, and have their highest bonus in the slash style; however, the [[blue moon spear]] is a two-handed weapon that is best at stab, has a slower attack speed of 5, and has good bonuses in all 3 melee styles.

Most bladed staves are variants of the [[staff of the dead]], which have the rare ability to [[autocast]] both [[Crumble Undead]] and [[Magic Dart]], and each can cast one of the [[god spells]] depending on the variant.

