{{External|rs|rsc}} {{Infobox Item |name = Blamish snail slime |image = [[File:Blamish snail slime.png]] |release = [[27 February]] [[2002]] |update = Latest RuneScape News (27 February 2002) |members = Yes |quest = [[Heroes' Quest]] |tradeable = No |equipable = No |stackable = No |noteable = No |options = Drop |examine = Yuck. |value = 5 |weight = 0.025 |id = 1581 }} [[File:Blamish snail slime detail.png|left|100px]] '''Blamish snail slime''' is a [[quest item]] in [[Heroes' Quest]]. When added to a [[vial of water]] with [[Harralander]] it makes [[blamish oil]], which can be used on a [[fishing rod]] to make an [[oily fishing rod]]. The oily fishing rod can then be used to catch [[lava eel]]s in the [[Taverley Dungeon]] or the [[Lava Maze]], or [[infernal eel]]s in [[Mor Ul Rek]].
Blamish snail slime can be made by going to [[Mort Myre Swamp]], killing a [[Myre blamish snail]], and grinding the raw snail ([[thin snail|thin]], [[lean snail|lean]], and [[fat snail|fat]] all work equally) with a [[pestle and mortar]] with an empty [[sample bottle]] in the player's inventory. Sample bottles can be obtained from the [[general store]] in [[Canifis]] or from [[Rasolo the Wandering Merchant]].
[[Gerrant]] provides players with blamish snail slime for free during Heroes' Quest.
