===Hybrid method===
By taking advantage of the [[coal bag]], it is possible to combine the smelting of [[gold ore]] with [[Mithril ore|mithril]], [[Adamantite ore|adamantite]], or [[runite ore]]. This method allows for time-efficient trips for players who wish to reduce the cost of goldsmithing at the Blast Furnace without greatly reducing experience per hour, or for players wishing to add additional experience per hour to traditional single-bar, mithril+ money-making methods at the Blast Furnace. 

The method is relatively simple to execute. An inventory consists of a [[coal bag]], [[goldsmith gauntlets]] or [[ice gloves]] (the other pair being equipped), and 26 gold, mithril, adamantite, or runite ore. Each time a full inventory of gold ore (26) is added to the Blast Furnace, the player will also transport and deposit 26 coal with the coal bag. Every few trips, depending on the ore that is being smelted, the player will forgo an inventory of gold ore to deposit an inventory of the other ore of their choosing. This will occur every two, three, or four trips depending on if the ore is mithril, adamantite, or runite, respectively. There is a small inconvenience, though: the coal bag holds 27 coal, not 26, so upon depositing ore at the conveyor belt, there will be 1 leftover coal in the bag. When banking later, this will cause the option available on the bag to be "empty" rather than "fill", which can cause players to think they have filled up their bag, when they emptied it instead. So, players must remember to either click '''twice''' on the coal bag in the banking interface (once to empty the 1 coal, another to fill up the bag) or use the "empty containers" option next to deposit inventory or alternatively empty out the remaining 1 coal and deposit it at the conveyor belt each trip.

