{{External|rs=Blessed hatchet}} {{Infobox Item |name = Blessed axe |image = [[File:Blessed axe.png]] |release = [[12 December]] [[2006]] |update = Animal Magnetism |members = Yes |quest = [[Animal Magnetism]] |tradeable = No |equipable = Yes |stackable = No |noteable = No |options = Wield, Destroy |destroy = I can obtain a replacement axe from the Burthorpe Slayer Master. |examine = It radiates purity but can still lop off heads. |value = 20 |weight = 1.162 |id = 10491 }} [[File:Blessed axe detail.png|left|130px]] The '''blessed axe''' is an axe made by [[Turael]] by giving him a [[mithril axe]] and a [[holy symbol]], which requires completing the [[Animal Magnetism]] quest up until the point [[Ava]] suggests talking to him. Talking to Turael after this step will then make it. It is used to chop [[undead twigs]] from the undead trees within the vicinity of [[Draynor Manor]]. Turael will make additional blessed axes if the required materials are brought to him again in [[Burthorpe]].
As the axe possesses a silver blade, it can damage [[vampyre]]s.
The blessed axe does not retain the functionality of the mithril axe used to create it; it cannot be used to chop anything but undead trees. It does not require an [[Attack]] level to wield. The only statistical difference is the blessed axe has a +2 [[Prayer]] bonus the mithril axe does not.
Despite being made with a holy symbol, the blessed axe does not count as a Saradomin item for [[God Wars Dungeon]] when equipped.
