{{Otheruses|blessed bones made from normal [[Bones]]|other types|Blessed bones (disambiguation)}} {{Infobox Item |name = Blessed bones |image = [[File:Blessed bones.png]] |release = [[20 March]] [[2024]] |update = Varlamore: Part One |members = Yes |quest = No |tradeable = No |equipable = No |stackable = No |noteable = No |options = Break-down, Drop |examine = Bones blessed at an exposed altar. |value = 1 |weight = 0.500 |id = 29344 }} [[File:Blessed bones detail.png|130px|left]] '''Blessed bones''' are the blessed form of [[bones]] obtained by using them on the [[exposed altar]] on the summit of [[Ralos' Rise]]. They are broken down with a [[chisel]] to obtain 4 [[blessed bone shards]] and 5 [[Crafting]] experience, which can then be sacrificed at the [[libation bowl]] at [[the Teomat]].
As each shard sacrificed gives 5 [[Prayer]] experience, each blessed bone gives 20 Prayer experience overall. If using a [[jug of blessed sunfire wine]] at the libation bowl instead of a regular [[jug of blessed wine]], this is increased to 6 Prayer experience per shard, or 24 Prayer experience per bone.
Players looking to bless bones in bulk may talk to [[Virilis]], found at the base of the exposed altar, to unnote any type of [[bones]] for a fee of 10 [[coins]] per bone.
