{{Infobox Item |defver = 2 |version1 = 1 use |version2 = 2 uses |bucketname1 = (1) |bucketname2 = (2) |name1 = Blessed crystal scarab (1) |name2 = Blessed crystal scarab (2) |image1 = [[File:Blessed crystal scarab (1).png]] |image2 = [[File:Blessed crystal scarab (2).png]] |release = [[24 August]] [[2022]] |update = Tombs of Amascut |members = Yes |quest = No |tradeable = Yes |equipable = No |stackable = No |noteable = Yes |options = Crack, Drop |examine = Restores a large amount of prayer over time. |value = 30 |weight = 0.453 |id1 = 27337 |id2 = 27335 }} {{Synced switch |version1 = [[File:Blessed crystal scarab (1) detail.png|left|120px]] |version2 = [[File:Blessed crystal scarab (2) detail.png|left|120px]] }} '''Blessed crystal scarabs''' are an item that can be obtained from the [[Supplies (Tombs of Amascut)|supplies bag]] within the [[Tombs of Amascut]].
Cracking it will restore a player's Prayer points by 8 points every 4 ticks (2.4 seconds) 9 times, for a total restoration of 72 Prayer points over the course of 40 ticks (24 seconds).
{{Tombs of Amascut}}

{{Infobox Item |name = Blessed dragon bones |image = [[File:Blessed dragon bones.png]] |release = [[20 March]] [[2024]] |update = Varlamore: Part One |members = Yes |quest = No |tradeable = No |equipable = No |stackable = No |noteable = No |options = Break-down, Drop |examine = Bones blessed at an exposed altar. |value = 160 |weight = 1.500 |id = 29356 }} [[File:Blessed dragon bones detail.png|130px|left]] '''Blessed dragon bones''' are the blessed form of [[dragon bones]] obtained by using them on the [[exposed altar]] on the summit of [[Ralos' Rise]]. They are broken down with a [[chisel]] to obtain 58 [[blessed bone shards]] and 5 [[Crafting]] experience, which can then be sacrificed at the [[libation bowl]] at [[the Teomat]].
As each shard sacrificed gives 5 [[Prayer]] experience, each blessed bone gives 290 Prayer experience overall. If using a [[jug of blessed sunfire wine]] at the libation bowl instead of a regular [[jug of blessed wine]], this is increased to 6 Prayer experience per shard, or 348 Prayer experience per bone.
Players looking to bless bones in bulk may talk to [[Virilis]], found at the base of the exposed altar, to unnote any type of [[bones]] for a fee of 10 [[coins]] per bone.
