{{External|rs=Wilderness North Volcano}} {{Infobox Location |name = Blighted Volcano |image = [[File:Wilderness Volcano.png|300px]] |release = [[24 April]] [[2006]] |update = Wilderness graphical update |aka = Wilderness volcano |members = Yes |location = [[Wilderness]] |wilderness = 55-56 |map = {{Map|name=Wilderness Volcano|x=3365|y=3935|zoom=2}} |type = volcano |leagueRegion = Wilderness }} {{Relative location |location = Blighted Volcano |north = Untamed Ocean |east = Fossil Island |south = Fountain of Rune |west = Rogues' Castle }} The '''Blighted Volcano''' is a small volcanic outcrop in the north-eastern section of the [[Wilderness]]. While walking around it, the ground will shake periodically - probably because of heavy volcanic activity. There is a rope bridge that spans the central pool of lava that can be crossed.
Like near the [[Chaos Temple (Wilderness)|Chaos Temple]], balls of fire shoot out of the pools of lava. If one hits a player, it can inflict minor damage. The volcano can be used to flee from the powerful [[Chaos Elemental]] that resides nearby to the west of the [[Rogues' Castle]]. Apart from this, the volcano has no use except for forging [[Odium ward|Odium]] and [[Malediction ward]]s, and being a sinister piece of scenery well suited to the hostile landscape of the Wilderness.
==Transportation== The volcano is located in the north east of the Wilderness, near [[Rogues' castle]] and the [[Fountain of Rune]]. *After completion of the [[Wilderness_Diary#Hard|hard Wilderness diary]], set the [[Wilderness Obelisk]] to level 50 Wilderness, teleport, and walk north-east. Alternatively, activate the obelisk until the level 50 obelisk is randomly chosen as the destination. *After completion of the [[Wilderness_Diary#Hard|hard Wilderness diary]], teleport with the [[Wilderness sword]] to the [[Fountain of Rune]] and head north. *Use [[Annakarl teleport]] or its corresponding [[Annakarl teleport (tablet)|tablet]] and head north-east. *From the [[Edgeville lever]], run east, past the [[Rogues' Castle]], to reach the volcano.
==Volcanic Forge== {{Main|Volcanic Forge}} The centre of the volcano houses a powerful forge, where players must travel to in order to combine the three shards of either the [[Malediction ward]] or [[Odium ward]]. When using one of the three shards on the Volcanic Forge, a message appears in the game tab stating ''You forge the shield pieces together in the chambers of fire and are blown back by the intense heat.'' [[File:Using Volcanic Forge.gif|frame|none|A player combines three shards, creating a ward.|136x136px]] {{Clear}}
==Wrecked ship== The north-western side of the volcano has a wrecked ship (possibly made out of metal, explaining why it hasn't burnt up due to the volcano. The ship cannot be explored and has no use other than for scenery. A large amount of skeletons litter the area, especially around the ship, seeming to indicate that the crew were either thrown from the ship during the crash and subsequently died from their injuries, or else that the crew attempted to flee and were then killed by lava.
One of the examine texts for these skeletons reads "A victim of war... looks like he's been dead for a while now.", implying this ship and its crew, if not the volcano itself, may have taken part in a notable event from [[Gielinor|Gielinor]]'s past, such as the [[God Wars]]. Next to the ship is an extension of the land on which eighteen [[Game square|squares]] are level 56 Wilderness - the deepest anyone can go.
[[File:Wilderness Volcano ship.png|thumb|319x319px|The mysterious wrecked ship in the northern part of the volcano.|none]] {{Clear}}
==Changes== {{Subject changes header}} {{Subject changes |date = 5 November 2025 |update = Sailing Technical Pre-Release |change = The location was labelled "Blighted Volcano" on the [[world map]]. }} {{Subject changes footer}}
==Trivia== [[File:Using gold ring on forge.gif|frame|A [[goblin (race)|goblin]] appears as the player uses a [[gold ring]] on the Volcanic Forge.]] *Using a [[gold ring]] on the Volcanic Forge results in a [[goblin (race)|goblin]] appearing, yelling "My Precious!!! NOOOOO!!!", referencing the character Gollum from ''{{Wp|The Lord of the Rings}}''. *Curiously, the wooden bridge across the volcano exists even though the constant lava splashes would have burnt and destroyed it. *A [[Clue scroll (hard) - Panic on the Wilderness volcano bridge|hard clue scroll step]] refers to the Blighted Volcano as the "Wilderness volcano".
{{Terrain}} {{Wilderness}} [[Category:Terrain]]

{{Infobox Item |name = Blighted ancient ice sack |image = [[File:Blighted ancient ice sack.png]] |release = [[23 April]] [[2020]] |update = Bounty Hunter Returns |members = Yes |quest = No |tradeable = Yes |equipable = No |stackable = Yes |noteable = No |options = Drop |examine = Enough power for any Ice spell, blighted so it can be used only in the Wilderness. |value = 35 |weight = 0.000 |exchange = Yes |id = 24607 }} [[File:Blighted ancient ice sack detail.png|left|120px]] '''Blighted ancient ice sacks''' are an item that allows players to cast any [[ice spells|ice spell]] within their [[Magic]] level without needing the [[runes]] for it. However, it can only be used inside the [[Wilderness]], [[Ferox Enclave]], [[Mage Arena bank]], [[PvP world]]s, [[Castle Wars]], [[Clan Wars]], and [[Soul Wars]], and the [[Ancient Magicks]] spellbook must be active.
30 can be purchased at [[Justine's stuff for the Last Shopper Standing]] for 1 [[Last Man Standing]] point or at the [[Soul Wars Reward Shop]] for 10 [[Zeal Tokens]].
Blighted ancient ice sacks function like runes, meaning having one in the inventory allows an ice spell to be cast via the spellbook. This also means [[autocast]]ing with Ancient Magicks staves is an option.
==Item sources== {{Drop sources|Blighted ancient ice sack}}
