{{Infobox Item |name = Blighted anglerfish |image = [[File:Blighted anglerfish.png]] |release = [[23 April]] [[2020]] |update = Bounty Hunter Returns |members = Yes |quest = No |tradeable = Yes |equipable = No |stackable = No |noteable = Yes |edible = Yes |options = Eat, Drop |examine = An unappetising fish, now blighted so it can be eaten only in the Wilderness. |value = 50 |weight = 0.400 |exchange = Yes |id = 24592 }} [[File:Blighted anglerfish detail.png|left|150px]] '''Blighted anglerfish''' are a variant of [[anglerfish]] that can only be eaten while inside the [[Wilderness]], [[Ferox Enclave]], [[Mage Arena bank]], [[PvP world|PvP Worlds]], [[Castle Wars]] lobby, and [[Clan Wars]]. 15 can be purchased at [[Justine's stuff for the Last Shopper Standing]] for 1 [[Last Man Standing]] point or at the [[Soul Wars Reward Shop]] for 10 [[Zeal Tokens]].
Similar to [[anglerfish]], blighted anglerfish can heal above maximum Hitpoints (making the maximum Hitpoints possible 121). Overheal does '''not''' apply if the player is in combat in a PvP area, whether with another player or a non-player character.
When attempting to eat the anglerfish outside the Wilderness, the message {{mes|The blighted anglerfish can be eaten only in the Wilderness.}} is displayed.
The message {{Mes|You eat the anglerfish. It heals some health.}} is shown when eating the blighted anglerfish inside the Wilderness.
The amount of Hitpoints boosted from eating anglerfish follows this table: {| class="wikitable" !{{SCP|Hitpoints|link=yes}} level !Health boost |- |1-19||3 |- |20-24||4 |- |25-29||6 |- |30-39||7 |- |40-49||8 |- |50-59||11 |- |60-69||12 |- |70-74||13 |- |75-79||15 |- |80-89||16 |- |90-92||17 |- |93-99||22 |}
==Formula for healing== The health boosted/restored seems to follow this formula: <math>\Delta Health = \lfloor Level \times \frac{1}{10} \rfloor + C</math>
Where Level is your base [[Hitpoints]] level and ''C'' is a variable, which differs depending on your Hitpoints level as the following table shows: {| class="wikitable" !{{SCP|Hitpoints|link=yes}} level !C |- |1-24||2 |- |25-49||4 |- |50-74||6 |- |75-92||8 |- |93-99||13 |}
