{{External|rs}} {{Infobox Item |name = Blisterwood sickle |image = [[File:Blisterwood sickle.png]] |release = [[4 June]] [[2020]] |update = Darkmeyer |members = Yes |quest = [[Sins of the Father]] |tradeable = No |equipable = Yes |stackable = No |noteable = No |options = Wield, Cast Bloom, Drop |wornoptions = Bloom |examine = A ruby sickle with a blade of silver and blisterwood. |value = 20000 |alchable = No |weight = 1.587 |id = 24697 }} [[File:Blisterwood sickle detail.png|left|150px]] The '''blisterwood sickle''' is an item obtained by using a [[ruby]] on a [[silver sickle (b)]], casting [[Lvl-3 Enchant]] on the resulting [[ruby sickle (b)]], and then using [[blisterwood logs]] on the [[enchanted ruby sickle (b)]]. It is used on the [[Ivandis flail]] to create the [[blisterwood flail]]. It requires an [[Attack]] level of 50 to wield.
The sickle has a right-click "bloom" option which can be used next to rotten logs, branches, or bushes in [[Mort Myre]] swamp to obtain [[Mort myre fungi]], [[Mort myre stem|stems]], and [[Mort myre pear|pears]]. These items can be used to fill the [[Druid pouch]] which allows the player to fight [[Ghast]]s. Bloom can also be cast on [[Dead vine (scenery)|dead vines]] in the [[Ancient Guthixian Temple]] to grow them into [[Vine flower (scenery)|flowering vines]] which can be picked to obtain a [[vine flower]].
It has a 15% damage and 5% accuracy bonus against [[vampyre]]s.{{CiteTwitter|author=Mod Ed|url=https://twitter.com/JagexEd/status/1269930624003059712|date=8 June 2020|archiveurl=https://reldo.runescape.wiki/i/103301|archivedate=8 June 2020|quote=Sickle is 15% damage and 5% accuracy.}}
