{{External|rs}} {{Infobox Item |name = Bloated toad |image = [[File:Bloated toad.png]] |release = [[18 May]] [[2004]] |update = Big Chompy Bird Hunting |members = Yes |quest = [[Big Chompy Bird Hunting]] |tradeable = No |bankable = No |equipable = No |stackable = No |noteable = No |options = Drop, Release All, Release |examine = An inflated toad. |value = 1 |weight = 0.750 |id = 2875 }} [[File:Bloated toad detail.png|left|130px]] '''Bloated toads''' are used to catch [[chompy bird]]s during and after the [[Big Chompy Bird Hunting]] [[quest]]. Their dyed variant, [[coloured toads]], are used during [[Mourning's End Part I]]. Bloated toads can be obtained by using [[ogre bellows]] which have been filled with swamp gas on a [[swamp toad]]. Only three toads may be obtained at one time, and they cannot be [[bank]]ed.
Bloated toads may only be dropped in the ogre areas east and south of [[Gu'Tanoth]]. Once dropped, they have a chance of causing a chompy bird to land, lasting 1 minute before exploding and dealing 1-2 damage to all players within one tile (including diagonally). This damage cannot kill players.
Inflating a toad a second time by using filled ogre bellows on a bloated toad will lead to the toad floating away in a comical manner if the player is not in the possession of a [[ball of wool]] and a [[Rock (elemental)|suitable rock]]; if these materials are available, however, a [[balloon toad]] will be created instead. ==Spawn mechanics== When placed on the ground, the bloated toad will roll every 25 ticks (15 seconds) for a chance to spawn a chompy bird, and will continue doing so until it either bursts or successfully attracts a bird.{{CiteTwitter|author=Mod Ash|url=https://twitter.com/JagexAsh/status/1148168402642579456|date=8 July 2019|archiveurl=https://archive.ph/ZH80H|archivedate=1 November 2022|quote=One toad does not influence the outcome of any other toad. The game tries spawning one from the toad at 15 sec intervals until the toad vanishes.}}{{CiteTwitter|author=Mod Ash|url=https://twitter.com/JagexAsh/status/1152244840534618113|date=19 July 2019|archiveurl=https://archive.ph/bKLf5|archivedate=1 November 2022|quote=The toad periodically rolls a chance of spawning a bird, until either it's succeeded in doing so, or it bursts.}} There is a 1 in 5 chance that a bloated toad attracts a chompy bird each time a roll is made, and up to four rolls can be carried out before a toad bursts.{{CiteDiscord|author=Mod Lenny|url=https://discord.com/channels/177206626514632704/269673599554551808/1082679278178672670|date=7 March 2023|quote=[hey lenny is there a 1/5 chance for a chompy to spawn every 25 ticks] looks right to me|archiveurl=https://reldo.runescape.wiki/i/27963014#chat-messages-269673599554551808-1082679278178672670|archivedate=9 March 2026}} Once a bloated toad has successfully attracted a chompy bird however, it will not attempt to spawn any additional ones.{{CiteTwitter|author=Mod Ash|url=https://twitter.com/JagexAsh/status/1591140915091238912|date=11 November 2022|archiveurl=https://archive.is/uohcs|archivedate=4 March 2023|quote=After it's done its spawning, it won't ever spawn more as far as I know.}} Therefore, a toad will fail to attract a chompy if it fails all four rolls, which works out to about a 41% failure rate. Conversely, players can expect a chompy bird to spawn in around 59% of cases.
{| class="wikitable align-right-1 align-center-2" !Moment !Spawn chance |- |25th tick |{{yes|20%}} |- |50th tick |{{yes|16%}} |- |75th tick |{{yes|12.8%}} |- |100th tick |{{yes|10.24%}} |- |No spawn |{{no|40.96%}} |}
Each bloated toad rolls independently of any other toads that may be placed nearby, and the chance to call down a chompy is likewise not influenced in any way by the proximity of the player to the toad.{{CiteTwitter|author=Mod Ash|url=https://twitter.com/JagexAsh/status/984176368811495424|date=11 April 2018|archiveurl=https://archive.ph/KUR7a|archivedate=1 November 2022|quote=It doesn't check where you are at all.}} If a bird is successfully lured in, it will land on a random empty tile somewhere between 3 and 10 tiles removed from the bloated toad, forming a 21x21 square spawn area.{{CiteTwitter|author=Mod Ash|url=https://twitter.com/JagexAsh/status/681917441056878592|date=29 December 2015|archiveurl=https://archive.ph/0r4W2|archivedate=1 November 2022|quote=The game looks for a random empty tile between 3-10 away from the toad.}} The landing tile must also have line-of-sight to the bloated toad.{{CiteTwitter|author=Mod Ash|url=https://twitter.com/JagexAsh/status/1591392818647662593|date=12 November 2022|archiveurl=https://archive.ph/rub9a|archivedate=2 June 2023|quote=It's got a random chance of not spawning one at all. If it sets out to spawn one, though, it'll try to find a tile with LoS as you say. It'd likely succeed unless the toad is somewhere very enclosed.}}
Although no more than three toads can be held in the inventory, there is no limit to how many toads may be placed on the ground simultaneously.{{CiteTwitter|author=Mod Ash|url=https://twitter.com/JagexAsh/status/1280239815074725888|date=6 July 2020|archiveurl=https://archive.ph/TAoJP|archivedate=4 March 2023|quote=I don't know of a capped limit on how many you can usefully place.}} As chompy birds will only attempt to devour the toads that spawned them down, and no more rolls are performed by the corresponding toads, it makes no meaningful difference whether the player actively prevents spawned chompy birds from eating the bait or not.
==Products== {{Uses material list|Bloated toad}}
==Messages== A number of messages are displayed or said by the player when interacting with bloated toads: {| class="wikitable" !Action !Message |- |Attempting to bank the toad |{{mes|A magical force prevents you from banking this item!}} |- |Trying to inflate a fourth toad |{{mes|One of your bloated toads manages to escape.}} |- |Trying to place multiple toads on the same tile |{{mes|There is a bloated toad already placed at this location.}} |- |Attempting to drop a toad outside the [[Feldip Hills|Feldip hills]] |{{mes|You won't attract a chompy bird this far away from the ogre area.}} |- |Inflating an already-bloated toad |{{mes|You manage to inflate a bloated toad with the swamp gas.}} |- |Releasing a toad from the inventory |{{overhead|Free the fatsy toady!}} (said by the player) |- |Inflating an un-bloated toad |{{overhead|Come here toady!}} (said by the player) |}
