{{Infobox Item |version1 = Normal |version2 = Broken |version3 = Locked |name1 = Blood ancient sceptre |name2 = Blood ancient sceptre (broken) |name3 = Blood ancient sceptre (l) |image1 = [[File:Blood ancient sceptre.png]] |image2 = [[File:Blood ancient sceptre (broken).png]] |image3 = [[File:Blood ancient sceptre.png]] |release1 = [[26 July]] [[2023]] |release2 = [[26 July]] [[2023]] |release3 = [[16 August]] [[2023]] |update1 = Desert Treasure II - The Fallen Empire |update2 = Desert Treasure II - The Fallen Empire |update3 = Desert Treasure II Changes & More |members = Yes |quest = No |tradeable = No |equipable1 = Yes |equipable2 = No |equipable3 = Yes |stackable = No |noteable = No |options1 = Wield, Dismantle, Drop |options2 = Drop |options3 = Wield, Drop |examine = A very old and powerful stick, enhanced with the power of blood magic. |value1 = 200000 |value2 = 1 |value3 = 200000 |alchable = No |weight = 2.267 |id1 = 28260 |id2 = 28238 |id3 = 28473 }} {{Synced switch |version1 = [[File:Blood ancient sceptre detail.png|left|150px]] |version2 = [[File:Blood ancient sceptre (broken) detail.png|left|150px]] |version3 = [[File:Blood ancient sceptre detail.png|left|150px]] }} The '''blood ancient sceptre''' is a sceptre requiring 75 [[Magic]], 60 [[Strength]], and 50 [[Attack]] to wield. It is made by attaching the [[blood quartz]], dropped by [[Vardorvis]], to the [[ancient sceptre]]; this process can be reversed, allowing players to switch between quartzes as desired.
Like its predecessor, it will increase the effects of [[Ancient Magicks]] by 10%, with the added effect of being able to overheal up to 10% over the player's base [[Hitpoints]].
The blood ancient sceptre finds practical use in the [[Inferno]] for improved [[Blood Barrage]]s at the end of waves, to start the next wave at up to 108 Hitpoints, as well as against [[God Wars Dungeon]] boss bodyguards in between boss kills.
If the player dies below level 20 [[Wilderness]], it will remain in the player's inventory; however, the item will be unusable and must be repaired by using it on [[Perdu]] and paying him {{NoCoins|{{GEP|Ancient staff}}+200000}}. If not protected when the player dies at level 20 Wilderness or higher, the sceptre is converted into [[coins]]. Alternatively, a [[Trouver parchment]] and a payment of 500,000 coins can be given to [[Perdu]] in order to lock it (after which it gains the (l) suffix); this allows the item to be kept in death, unbroken, even if the player dies at level 20 Wilderness or higher.
