{{Infobox Monster |name = Blood jaguar |image = [[File:Blood jaguar.png|280px]] |release = [[20 March]] [[2024]] |update = Varlamore: Part One |members = Yes |combat = 40 |size = 2 |examine = Bloody oversized cats... |xpbonus = |max hit = 5 |aggressive = Yes |poisonous = No |attack style = [[Crush]] |attack speed = 6 |hitpoints = 100 |att = 40 |str = 40 |def = 28 |mage = 1 |range = 1 |attbns = 0 |strbns = 0 |amagic = 0 |mbns = 0 |arange = 0 |rngbns = 0 |dstab = 0 |dslash = 0 |dcrush = 0 |dmagic = 0 |dlight = 0 |dstandard = 0 |dheavy = 0 |elementalweaknesstype = Earth |elementalweaknesspercent = 15 |poisonresistance = 100 |venomresistance = 100 |immunecannon = Yes |freezeresistance = 100 |id = 13021 }} '''Blood jaguars''' are an NPC summoned by the [[Blood Moon]] as one of her special attacks. They will spawn as multiple in a circle around the boss, with one standing in front of [[Eyatlalli]]'s glyph, which is the one players can attack. While they are attacking, a damaging square of blood pools will continually spawn around the Blood Moon.
In order to avoid damage, players must step away from the jaguar prior to its attack, as they remain stationary, as well as timing it correctly to avoid the blood pools. Approximately 20% of the damage dealt to a jaguar will heal the player. Once a player has regained 20 Hitpoints total, hitting the jaguar will stop restoring Hitpoints unless more damage is taken. [[File:Blood Moon - dodging blood jaguars.mp4|thumb|left|400px|The player moves away right before the blood jaguar attacks. The cue to dodge the jaguar can be heard from the end of the blood pool sound effect, or looking at the blood splat until it has fully formed.]]
==Changes== {{Subject changes header}} {{Subject changes |date = 25 June 2025 |update = Summer Sweep Up: Combat |change = Blood jaguars now have a 15% [[elemental weakness]] to [[earth spells]]. }} {{Subject changes footer}}
{{Neypotzli}}

[[File:Blood moon helm chathead.png|left]]
[[File:Bloodrager.gif|thumb|280px|A player triggers the ''Bloodrager'' set effect.]]
'''Blood moon armour''' is a set of melee equipment which requires level 75 [[Strength]] and 50 [[Defence]] to equip, which is obtained as a possible reward from the [[Lunar Chest]] in [[Neypotzli]].

The chest and legs have the same strength bonus as [[Bandos armour]], making it very popular for mid-level players due to its cheap cost and accessibility. The defensive bonuses are much weaker than those of Bandos armour, except its slash defence (which is only slightly lower) and magic defence, which is significantly higher. It is also much lower in [[weight]].

==Set effect==
'''Bloodrager:''' The [[dual macuahuitl]] has a 33% chance upon a [[successful hit]] to attack one [[tick]] earlier than usual, allowing the player to attack again after 3 ticks. Both hits count towards this independently{{CiteVideo|name=maracas|site=youtube|title=Fortis Colosseum & Perilous Moons Q&A Livestream!|timestamp=2253s|author=Old School RuneScape|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=n9py_1vGiMQ&t=2253s|date=27 October 2023}}, meaning there is a 5/9 (56%) chance to trigger the effect if both hits are successful. 70 [[Attack]] and 75 [[Strength]] are required to equip this two-handed weapon.

It is possible for the set effect to activate even if one or more of the armour pieces are broken.

