{{Item set}}

{{Infobox Item |version1 = New |version2 = Used |version3 = Broken |name1 = Blood moon chestplate |name2 = Blood moon chestplate |name3 = Blood moon chestplate (broken) |image1 = [[File:Blood moon chestplate.png]] |image2 = [[File:Blood moon chestplate (used).png]] |image3 = [[File:Blood moon chestplate (broken).png]] |release = [[20 March]] [[2024]] |update = Varlamore: Part One |members = Yes |quest = No |tradeable1 = Yes |tradeable2 = No |tradeable3 = Yes |equipable = Yes |stackable = No |noteable1 = Yes |noteable2 = No |noteable3 = Yes |options1 = Wear, Drop |options2 = Wear, Check, Drop |options3 = Drop |examine = The chestplate of the Blood Moon. |value = 290010 |weight = 5.443 |exchange1 = Yes |exchange2 = No |exchange3 = Yes |id1 = 29022 |id2 = 29043 |id3 = 29067 |leagueRegion = Varlamore }} {{Synced switch |version1 = [[File:Blood moon chestplate detail.png|140px|left]] |version2 = [[File:Blood moon chestplate (used) detail.png|140px|left]] |version3 = [[File:Blood moon chestplate (broken) detail.png|140px|left]] }} The '''blood moon chestplate''' is an item that requires level 75 [[Strength]] and 50 [[Defence]] to equip, which is obtained as a possible reward from the [[Lunar Chest]] in [[Neypotzli]]. With similar stats to a [[fighter torso]], it is tradeable and has identical strength bonus, while having +50 more magic defence bonus.
When worn with all of the other pieces of the [[blood moon armour]] set, the player gains the ''Bloodrager'' set effect, where the [[dual macuahuitl]] has a 33% chance to hit one [[tick]] sooner upon a [[successful hit]]; using the weapon's special attack guarantees the effect.
As with all [[Moon equipment]] it is degradeable, much like [[Barrows equipment]]. The armour starts at 3000 charges and loses 1 charge for every 54 seconds in combat, meaning it will last for 45 hours of continuous combat before breaking. Having an NPC such as [[Bob]] and [[Dunstan]] repair it costs 1,500,000 coins when fully broken, while repairing it yourself at an [[armour stand]] adds a discount of 7,500 coins per visible [[Smithing]] level. At level 99, the price is reduced to 757,500 coins.
