{{Infobox Item |name = Blood pint |image = [[File:Blood pint.png]] |release = [[4 June]] [[2020]] |update = Darkmeyer |members = Yes |quest = No |tradeable = Yes |equipable = No |stackable = No |noteable = Yes |options = Drink, Drop |examine = It's literally a pint of blood. |value = 2 |weight = 0.550 |respawn = 100 |exchange = Yes |id = 24774 }} [[File:Blood pint detail.png|left|130px]] '''Blood pint''' is a type of [[ale]] that [[Temporary skill boost|temporarily boosts]] [[Attack]] and [[Strength]] by 4% + 2 while [[Temporary skill drain|draining]] [[Magic]] and [[Prayer]] by 4% + 2 when drunk (see table below). Unlike other ales, it cannot be made through [[brewing]].
Upon drinking the ale, the message {{mes|You drink the Blood Pint. It tastes unsurprisingly awful and makes you feel a bit sick.}} will appear.
The blood pint '''cannot''' be used to create a [[vial of blood]] or [[Cadantine blood potion (unf)|unfinished cadantine blood potion]]: when combined with a [[vial]], the message {{mes|You try to fill your vial with blood but it spills all over the ground.}} appears, leaving the player with an empty [[beer glass]] and the empty vial, and when combined with a [[cadantine]], the message {{mes|Your standards are not low enough to try that.}} appears.
Blood pints, as well as [[Raw mystery meat|raw]] and [[Cooked mystery meat|cooked]] versions of mystery meat, can be given to [[Frank (Bloodveld)|Frank]].
==Effects== Stat buffs and debuffs are calculated with: <math>\lfloor SkillLevel \times \frac{4}{100} \rfloor + 2</math>
{| class="wikitable" style="text-align:center;" !{{SCP|Attack}} Level {{SCP|Strength}} !Boost !{{SCP|Attack}} Level {{SCP|Strength}} !Boost |- |'''1-24'''||+2||'''50-74'''||+4 |- |'''25-49'''||+3||'''75-99'''||+5 |- |}
{| class="wikitable" style="text-align:center;" !{{SCP|Prayer}} Level {{SCP|Magic}} !Boost !{{SCP|Prayer}} Level {{SCP|Magic}} !Boost |- |'''1-24'''||-2||'''50-74'''||-4 |- |'''25-49'''||-3||'''75-99'''||-5 |- |}
