{{otheruses|the NPC spawned by [[the Maiden of Sugadinti]]|the NPC spawned by [[Zebak]]|Blood Cloud}} {{Infobox Monster |version1 = Entry |version2 = Normal |name = Blood spawn |image = [[File:Blood spawn.png|200px]] |release = [[7 June]] [[2018]] |update = The Theatre of Blood |members = Yes |combat = 55 |size = 1 |examine = The power of blood. |xpbonus = 0 |max hit = 1 (does not attack) |aggressive = No |poisonous = No |attack style = None |attack speed = No |hitpoints1 = 7 |hitpoints2 = 120 |scaledhp = Yes |att = 1 |str = 1 |def = 0 |mage = 0 |range = 1 |attbns = 0 |strbns = 0 |amagic = 0 |mbns = 0 |arange = 0 |rngbns = 0 |dstab = 0 |dslash = 0 |dcrush = 0 |dmagic = 0 |dlight = 0 |dstandard = 0 |dheavy = 0 |elementalweaknesstype = Earth |elementalweaknesspercent = 50 |poisonresistance = 100 |venomresistance = 100 |id = 8367,10821,10829 }} '''Blood spawn''' are monsters that spawn during [[the Maiden of Sugadinti]] encounter in the [[Theatre of Blood]], in which up to eight can spawn. If players successfully avoid the Maiden's blood splat attack, a maximum of one blood spawn will appear.
They wander around the arena, creating a trail of blood which deal damage if stood upon. In [[Theatre of Blood/Entry Mode|entry mode]] the damage is 2 to 5, and in [[Theatre of Blood|normal mode]] the damage is 5 to 13.
Despite never attacking the player directly, casting [[Monster Examine]] will reveal that it has a stab attack style and a max hit of 1.
==Changes== {{Subject changes header}} {{Subject changes |date = 25 June 2025 |update = Summer Sweep Up: Combat |change = Blood spawns now have a 50% [[elemental weakness]] to [[earth spells]]. }} {{Subject changes |date = 12 August 2021 |update = Tombs of Amascut: Rewards Beta |poll = A Night At The Theatre and Old School Content Poll 75: PvM |change = There's now less variation in where the Maiden Blood Spawns appear. Additionally, if players successfully dodge the blood, a maximum of only one Blood Spawn will appear. }} {{Subject changes |date = 9 January 2020 |update = Eating in the Bank |poll = Old School Content Poll 69: Game Improvements |change = *The chance of blood spawns spawning are now halved if players successfully avoid the Maiden's blood splat attack. *The amount of blood spawns that can appear in the fight is now capped at eight. }} {{Subject changes footer}}
{{Theatre of Blood}}

{{External|rs}} {{Infobox Item |name = Blood talisman |image = [[File:Blood talisman.png]] |release = [[23 March]] [[2022]] |update = Guardians of the Rift Launch |members = Yes |quest = No |tradeable = Yes |equipable = No |stackable = No |noteable = Yes |options = Locate, Drop |examine = A mysterious power emanates from the talisman... |value = 4 |weight = 0.015 |exchange = Yes |id = 1450 |leagueRegion = Morytania }} [[File:Blood talisman detail.png|130px|left]] The '''blood talisman''' is a [[talisman]] that allows players to enter the [[Blood Altar]] where [[blood rune]]s are crafted. The Blood Altar is located in the [[Meiyerditch Laboratories]], which is discovered during [[Sins of the Father]]. Making [[blood rune]]s requires level 77 [[Runecraft]]. The talisman is not required to access [[Kourend]]'s [[Blood Altar (Kourend)|Blood Altar]], as it is not the true Blood Altar.
Blood talismans can be obtained from the [[Temple Supplies]] shop at the [[Guardians of the Rift]] minigame, granted the player has completed [[Sins of the Father]]. It can be combined with a [[tiara]] to make a [[blood tiara]] for 52.5 Runecraft [[experience]] at the Blood Altar, by using the tiara on the altar. This makes the talisman disappear, but the blood tiara can be used in just the same way and can be worn on the head, saving an inventory space when crafting blood runes.
Though it has a locate option, using it will give the message,{{Mes|The talisman doesn't seem to work. Maybe the ruins are deep underground.}} This message will persist even if the player is in the Meiyerditch Laboratories.
==Products== {{Uses material list|Blood talisman}}
==Store locations== {{Store locations list|Blood talisman}}
