==Trivia== * The blood talisman seems to have the ability to influence people to madness, as seen in the story told on the [[tatty note (Sins of the Father)|tatty note]] found in the blood altar; of a miner driven to stab his friend after coming into contact with the talisman. ** With the way the note is written, it is unclear whether the corrupting influence is the altar itself, the talisman, or both. * The blood talisman is referenced by the dwarf [[Thorgel]] in the [[Mourning's End Part II]] quest. Players take a [[item list|list of items]] to him in exchange for a [[death talisman]], but if you ask why he needs one of the three keys he asks you for, he will reply "''Pretty please with a Blood Talisman on top?!''", then you would say "''A Blood Talisman?!''", and then Thorgel would reply "''Oops! I meant 'Death Talisman'!''" with a shifty look on his face. * The blood talisman is an extremely rare example of an item that was present in the launch version of ''Old School RuneScape'' (in the game cache as an unobtainable item), removed from the game, and later re-added in a different update. ** It was initially removed due to the [[Blood Altar (Kourend)|false Blood Altar]] (which does not require a blood talisman) being added alongside the release of [[Great Kourend]], and it became accessible in-game for the first time with the release of [[Guardians of the Rift]] on 23 March 2022.
{{Guardians of the Rift}} {{Runecraft}}

{{External|rs}} {{Infobox Item |name = Blood tiara |image = [[File:Blood tiara.png]] |release = [[23 March]] [[2022]] |update = Guardians of the Rift Launch |members = Yes |quest = No |tradeable = Yes |equipable = Yes |stackable = No |noteable = Yes |options = Wear, Drop |examine = A tiara infused with the properties of blood. |value = 500 |weight = 1.000 |exchange = Yes |id = 5549 |leagueRegion = Morytania }} [[File:Blood tiara detail.png|left|130px]] [[File:Blood tiara chathead.png|left]] A '''blood tiara''' is a [[head slot]] item used in [[Runecraft]]. It is created at the [[Blood Altar]] by using a [[tiara]] or [[blood talisman]] on the altar with both in your inventory. This consumes the blood talisman and yields 52.5 Runecraft [[experience]]. Accessing the Blood Altar through [[Guardians of the Rift]] '''cannot''' be used for imbuement.
While a blood tiara is equipped, the [[mysterious ruins]] to the Blood Altar have a left-click "''Enter''" option, freeing up an inventory slot that the blood talisman would otherwise occupy.
