[[File:Bloodbark helm chathead.png|left]]
'''Bloodbark armour''' is a set of [[members]]-only [[Armour#Magic armour|magic armour]] that requires 60 [[Magic]] and 60 [[Defence]] to wear. Each piece of bloodbark armour can be made by using the corresponding piece of [[splitbark armour]] on either the true [[Blood Altar]] or [[Blood Altar (Kourend)|Kourend's Blood Altar]], and costs a certain amount of [[blood rune]]s. Infusing splitbark armour into bloodbark armour requires sufficient [[Runecraft]] skill, as well as having learned how to do so via reading the [[Runescroll of bloodbark]].
* The [[Bloodbark gauntlets|gauntlets]] and [[Bloodbark boots|boots]] require 100 blood runes each and 77 Runecraft.
* The [[Bloodbark helm|helm]] requires 250 blood runes and 79 Runecraft.
* The [[Bloodbark body|body]] and [[Bloodbark legs|legs]] require 500 blood runes each (1,000 runes total) and 81 Runecraft.

Thus, crafting a full Bloodbark armour set requires 1,450 blood runes.

The melee defence is comparable to [[adamant armour]] (and slightly better than that of [[Ahrim the Blighted's equipment|Ahrim's robes]]), and the total Magic bonus is 5 greater than that of [[mystic robes]]. The helm, body and legs each give a [[Magic damage]] bonus of 1% for a total of 3%. In addition to their stats, each piece of armour increases the amount that [[blood spells]] heal by 2% of the damage dealt. When the full set of armour is equipped, blood spells will heal the caster's [[Hitpoints]] for a total of 35% of the amount of damage inflicted.{{efn|As the amount of Hitpoints restored by a blood spell is first rounded down before the bonus of bloodbark armour is applied, the total healing effect might be lower in practice.{{CiteTwitter|author=Mod Ash|url=https://twitter.com/JagexAsh/status/1621586006301446145|date=3 February 2023|archiveurl=https://archive.is/pjufK|archivedate=21 March 2023|quote=The 1/4 calculation rounds down first. After that, the result is scaled up by the bloodbark effect, but you'd likely have lost quite a bit due to the initial rounding down.}}}} 

When worn alongside the [[Ancient sceptre]], the sceptre's passive 10% bonus to Ancient Magicks increases the total healing to 38.5% of the amount of damage inflicted.

When equipped together with the [[Zuriel staff]], its 50% passive bonus to Ancient Magicks raises the overall healing to 52.5% of the damage dealt.

It can be stored in a [[Magic wardrobe space|magic wardrobe]] in a player-owned house.

Despite the fact that the [[Sanguinesti staff]] uses blood magic for its built-in spell, bloodbark armour has no effect when used with it.

