{{Infobox Item |name = Bloodbark helm |image = [[File:Bloodbark helm.png]] |release = [[27 January]] [[2021]] |update = Shades of Mort'ton Rework |members = Yes |quest = No |tradeable = Yes |equipable = Yes |stackable = No |noteable = Yes |options = Wear, Drop |examine = A rather interesting smelling helmet. |value = 15000 |weight = 0.907 |exchange = Yes |id = 25413 }} [[File:Bloodbark helm detail.png|left|130px]] [[File:Bloodbark helm chathead.png|left]] A '''bloodbark helm''' is a piece of [[bloodbark armour]] worn in the [[headwear slot]], requiring level 60 [[Magic]] and 60 [[Defence]] to equip. The helm can be made with level 79 [[Runecraft]] by bringing a [[splitbark helm]] and 250 [[blood rune]]s to either the true [[Blood Altar]] or [[Blood Altar (Kourend)|Kourend's Blood Altar]]. Doing so requires players to have first learnt the secret to infuse the armour via reading the [[runescroll of bloodbark]].
Each piece of bloodbark armour equipped increases the amount that [[blood spells]] heal by 2%. When the full set of armour is equipped, blood spells will heal the caster's [[Hitpoints]] by 35% of the amount of damage inflicted. It can be stored in a [[magic wardrobe]] in a player-owned house.
