{{Infobox Item |name = Bloodbark legs |image = [[File:Bloodbark legs.png]] |release = [[27 January]] [[2021]] |update = Shades of Mort'ton Rework |members = Yes |quest = No |tradeable = Yes |equipable = Yes |stackable = No |noteable = Yes |options = Wear, Drop |examine = Strong leg protection. |value = 80000 |weight = 3.628 |exchange = Yes |id = 25416 }} [[File:Bloodbark legs detail.png|left|100px]] '''Bloodbark legs''' are a piece of [[bloodbark armour]] worn in the [[legs slot]], requiring level 60 [[Magic]] and 60 [[Defence]] to equip. The legs can be made with level 81 [[Runecraft]] by bringing a [[splitbark legs]] and 500 [[blood rune]]s to either the true [[Blood Altar]] or [[Blood Altar (Kourend)|Kourend's Blood Altar]]. Doing so requires players to have first learnt the secret to infuse the armour via reading the [[runescroll of bloodbark]].
Each piece of bloodbark armour equipped increases the amount that [[blood spells]] heal by 2%. When the full set of armour is equipped, blood spells will heal the caster's [[Hitpoints]] by 35% of the amount of damage inflicted. It can be stored in a [[magic wardrobe]] in a player-owned house.
