{{External|rs}} {{Infobox Monster |name = Bloodworm |image = [[File:Bloodworm.png|280px]] |release = [[9 May]] [[2005]] |update = Barrows |members = Yes |combat = 52 |size = 1 |examine = I think I should keep my distance... |xpbonus = 0 |max hit = 3 |aggressive = Yes |poisonous = No |attack style = [[Stab]] |attack speed = 4 |respawn = 50 |hitpoints = 45 |att = 80 |str = 20 |def = 35 |mage = 1 |range = 1 |attbns = 0 |strbns = 0 |amagic = 0 |mbns = 0 |arange = 0 |rngbns = 0 |dstab = 0 |dslash = 0 |dcrush = 0 |dmagic = 0 |dlight = 0 |dstandard = 0 |dheavy = 0 |poisonresistance = 0 |venomresistance = 0 |immunecannon = No |immunethrall = No |id = 1678 }} '''Bloodworms''' are a species of yellowish-reddish, [[leech]]-like creatures that lurk in the [[Barrows]] tunnels where they live in the darkness and feed on the blood of unwary treasure hunters. Bloodworms are one of the many obstacles between a player and the chest containing rewards where they constantly distract players from completing puzzles. As with all monsters in the crypts, they are [[aggressiveness|aggressive]] to any player regardless of their [[Combat level]]. They are commonly killed alongside two [[skeleton (Barrows)|skeletons]] each run as a quick way to optimise the player's reward potential for the most runes. They may [[spawn]] whenever the player opens a door in the tunnels.
