{{External|rs}}
[[File:Bloom.gif|300px|thumb|right|The animation of casting Bloom.]]
The '''Bloom''' [[spell]] is learned during the [[Nature Spirit]] [[quest]] when [[Filliman Tarlock]] asks for a [[silver sickle]], which he then blesses.

Every variant of the [[blessed silver sickle]] as well as the [[Ivandis flail]] and [[Blisterwood flail]] can be used to cast Bloom on [[small bush]]es, [[rotting log]]s, and [[rotting branch]]es in the [[Mort Myre Swamp]] to harvest [[Mort myre pear|pears]], [[Mort myre fungi|fungi]], and [[Mort myre stem|stems]] respectively. Bloom can also be cast while fighting [[swamp crab]]s, causing fungi to blossom from their shells, which will be dropped when they are slain. The [[druidic spell]] given to the player during Nature Spirit has a similar effect, but it is single-use and does not cost any Prayer points.

Bloom can also be cast on [[Dead vine (scenery)|dead vines]] in the [[Ancient Guthixian Temple]] to grow them into [[Vine flower (scenery)|flowering vines]] which can be picked to obtain a [[vine flower]].

No [[runes]] are required for this spell. The spell costs a random value of 1-6 [[Prayer|Prayer points]] to cast, and it cannot be cast at 0 Prayer points. [[Prayer]] may be recharged at the Nature Altar in the [[Nature Grotto]] where Filliman Tarlock lived.

The components created with the Bloom spell may be used in [[Herblore]] or may be added to a [[Druid pouch]], allowing [[Ghast]]s to become fully visible and subject to attack. A druid pouch can also be used on [[druid spirit]]s during [[While Guthix Sleeps]] to obtain potion ingredients used to progress the quest.

[[File:Mort Myre fungi collecting - Drakan's medallion method.png|thumb|left|300px|An ideal location to cast Bloom, north of [[Ver Sinhaza]].]]

