{{Otheruses|def=no|other uses|Blue moon (disambiguation)}} {{Instance}} {{HasStrategy|page=Moons of Peril/Strategies}} {{Infobox Monster |name = Blue Moon |image = [[File:Blue Moon.png|200px]] |release = [[20 March]] [[2024]] |update = Varlamore: Part One |members = Yes |combat = 329 |size = 5 |examine = The icy embodiment of a blue moon. |xpbonus = 17.5 |flatarmour = -5 |max hit = 32 total [4+8+20] |aggressive = Yes |poisonous = No |attack style = [[Typeless]] [[slash]] |attack speed = 6 |hitpoints = 500 |att = 258 |str = 100 |def = 60 |mage = 100 |range = 1 |attbns = 100 |strbns = 0 |amagic = 0 |mbns = 0 |arange = 0 |rngbns = 0 |dstab = 100 |dslash = 100 |dcrush = 0 |dmagic = 500 |dlight = 500 |dstandard = 500 |dheavy = 500 |elementalweaknesstype = Air |elementalweaknesspercent = 15 |poisonresistance = 100 |venomresistance = 100 |immunecannon = Yes |immuneburn = Immune to strong burns |freezeresistance = 100 |id = 13013 |leagueRegion = Varlamore }} The '''Blue Moon''' is one of the three [[Moons of Peril]] imprisoned in [[Neypotzli]]. She is one of the [[nagua]] -alongside the [[Blood Moon]] and [[Eclipse Moon]]- who were originally summoned by a powerful shaman facing imminent death. Her companions disapproved and created Neypotzli to imprison the Moons and keep them from inflicting harm.{{CiteNPC|npc=Eyatlalli|quote=In the face of inevitable death, a powerful shaman decided to lash out and inflict death on others. Her fellows disagreed with her actions. They created this prison, and they summoned me to watch over it.}}
The Blue Moon has a unique [[flat armour]] stat of -5, which increases the damage dealt against her by 5. As a result of this, weapons which deal damage via multiple hitsplats are particularly effective here.
If you are logged out or disconnect during the Weapon Freeze special attack, your weapon can be reclaimed from [[Eyatlalli]].
==Location== {{LocTableHead}} {{LocLine |name = Blue Moon |location = [[Neypotzli]] - Blue Moon chamber |levels = 329 |members = Yes |mapID = 45 |plane = 0 |x:1440,y:9680 |mtype = pin |leagueRegion = Varlamore }} {{LocTableBottom}}
==Fight overview== {{Main|Moons of Peril/Strategies#Boss mechanics}}
The boss' standard attacks are a series of three hits, rolling accuracy and damage against the player's melee defence. Once the boss misses one of the hits, the remaining hits in the stack will automatically miss. Not having enough defence and being hit by the boss will cause your hands to freeze, causing you to miss attacks.
After six standard attacks, she will use one of two special attacks, alternating between them: * '''Weapon Freeze''' - Your weapon is forcefully removed and placed in a block of ice, where you must punch the ice with Eyatlalli's glyph under it. Icy spikes will also periodically appear that must be avoided. * '''Frost Storm''' - Two braziers at the ends of the chamber are extinguished. Run to each and relight them, whilst avoiding the moving storms that deal damage and force you to walk for two ticks. The boss will also heal five times during the storm, restoring 10 health for each unlit brazier. Restoring both braziers will also remove a portion of stacks from Curse of the Moon. Stand in the sun symbol that rotates around the boss during regular attacks. Remaining outside the symbol will cause you to take increasing damage over time.
==Gallery== <gallery mode="packed" heights="150"> Blue Moon - idle animation.mp4|autoplay|loop|The Blue Moon's idle animation, by [[Mod Hend]]. Blue Moon - special attack animation.mp4|autoplay|loop|The Blue Moon's special attack animation, by Mod Hend. Blue Moon - death animation.mp4|autoplay|loop|The Blue Moon's death animation, by Mod Hend. Fighting the Blue Moon.png|A group of players fighting the Blue Moon of Peril. </gallery>
==Changes== {{Subject changes header}} {{Subject changes |update = Varlamore & Summer Sweep-Up Combat Tweaks |date = 6 August 2025 |change = The number of tornadoes spawned by the Blue Moon has been further reduced. }} {{Subject changes |date = 25 June 2025 |update = Summer Sweep Up: Combat |change = * The Blue Moon now has a 15% [[elemental weakness]] to [[wind spells]]. * The Blue Moon now spawns fewer tornadoes during their tornado attack. }} {{Subject changes |date = 3 April 2024 |update = Varlamore Tweaks & Drop Rates |change = * The [[ring of recoil]] now correctly loses charges against the boss. * Quick-escape is now the default option for the stairs in the boss' chamber. }} {{Subject changes |date = 27 March 2024 |update = Easter & Varlamore Updates |change = * The rate at which the Blue Moon boss builds cold has doubled. * The Blue Moon boss now heals more consistently during the tornado phase. }} {{Subject changes footer}}
