{{Infobox Scenery
|name = Bluefin shoal
|image = [[File:Bluefin shoal.png|290px]]
|release = [[19 November]] [[2025]]
|update = Sailing is OUT TODAY!
|members = Yes
|location = Varies
|options = Rod-fish
|examine = A shoal of bluefin.
|map = No
|id = 59738
|leagueRegion = No
}}
'''Bluefin shoals''' are a type of fish shoal found out at sea. They can be fished for [[raw bluefin]] via [[deep sea trawling]], requiring level 87 [[Fishing]] and granting 220.5 experience per successful catch with a [[trawling net]], or 44.1 if caught with a [[fishing rod]].

Unlike coastal fishing spots, players must use a [[boat]] to reach fish shoals and operate a trawling net within range of it, whilst matching the depth the shoal is currently swimming in. Bluefin shoals swim at shallow, moderate, and deep depths, and as such must be caught with a [[hemp trawling net]] or greater to consistently catch them.

While the shoal is moving to the next stop, they will always be at '''moderate''' depths. Upon stopping, they will swim to either '''shallow''' or '''deep''' depths, before swimming back to '''moderate''' depths once the timer reaches the halfway point.

Operating a trawling net is always preferred over rod fishing, as the latter requires the use of one [[fine fish offcut]] per fish, while the former uses it as optional bait to grant a 20% chance of catching an extra fish during a stop.

Regardless of the route chosen, Bluefin shoals always stop for {{ticks|70}} at specific points along their path.

