==Changes== {{Subject changes header}} {{Subject changes |date = 5 November 2025 |update = Sailing Technical Pre-Release |change = * The Smithing skill guide now correctly lists blurite bars as requiring level 13 to smelt. * Superheating blurite ore into blurite bars now requires 10 Smithing, up from 8 Smithing. }} {{Subject changes footer}}
==Trivia== * It is possible to smelt blurite with [[Superheat Item]] at 10 Smithing. Attempting to cast Superheat Item without 10 Smithing yields the message {{mes|You need a Smithing level of 10 to smelt blurite.}} ** Prior to 5 November 2025, it was possible to superheat blurite at 8 Smithing, which was reflected in the in-game guide. Attempting to cast Superheat Item without 8 Smithing at this time gave the message "You need a Smithing level of at least 8 to smelt Blurite Ore.". <!--used tbox instead of mes--> *Though other [[blurite]] equipment may be smithed from bars, [[Thurgo]] does not teach the player the ability to smith a [[blurite sword]].
{{Blurite}} {{Bar}}

{{External|rs|dw=Blurite Bolts}} {{Infobox Item |version1 = Unpoisoned |version2 = Poison |version3 = Poison+ |version4 = Poison++ |name1 = Blurite bolts |name2 = Blurite bolts (p) |name3 = Blurite bolts (p+) |name4 = Blurite bolts (p++) |image1 = [[File:Blurite bolts 1.png]] [[File:Blurite bolts 2.png]] [[File:Blurite bolts 3.png]] [[File:Blurite bolts 4.png]] [[File:Blurite bolts 5.png]] |image2 = [[File:Blurite bolts (p) 1.png]] [[File:Blurite bolts (p) 2.png]] [[File:Blurite bolts (p) 3.png]] [[File:Blurite bolts (p) 4.png]] [[File:Blurite bolts (p) 5.png]] |image3 = [[File:Blurite bolts (p+) 1.png]] [[File:Blurite bolts (p+) 2.png]] [[File:Blurite bolts (p+) 3.png]] [[File:Blurite bolts (p+) 4.png]] [[File:Blurite bolts (p+) 5.png]] |image4 = [[File:Blurite bolts (p++) 1.png]] [[File:Blurite bolts (p++) 2.png]] [[File:Blurite bolts (p++) 3.png]] [[File:Blurite bolts (p++) 4.png]] [[File:Blurite bolts (p++) 5.png]] |release = [[31 July]] [[2006]] |update = Crossbows |members = Yes |quest = No |tradeable = No |equipable = Yes |stackable = Yes |noteable = No |options = Wield, Drop |examine1 = Blurite crossbow bolts. |examine2 = Some poisoned blurite bolts. |examine3 = Some poisoned blurite bolts. |examine4 = Super poisoned blurite bolts. |value = 2 |weight = 0.000 |id1 = 9139 |id2 = 9286 |id3 = 9293 |id4 = 9300 }} {{Synced switch |version1 = [[File:Blurite bolts detail.png|left|130px]] |version2 = [[File:Blurite bolts (p) detail.png|left|130px]] |version3 = [[File:Blurite bolts (p) detail.png|left|130px]] |version4 = [[File:Blurite bolts (p) detail.png|left|130px]] }} '''Blurite bolts''' are the second weakest type of bolts. They are stronger than [[bronze bolts]] but weaker than [[iron bolts]]. They can only be fired from at least a [[blurite crossbow]] or better. As with most [[Bolt|bolts]], they can be [[Poison#Weapon poisoning|poisoned]], however this will prevent the addition of [[bolt tips]].
Blurite bolts cannot be bought, and can only be created by players. First, in order to make blurite bolts, a player must smith [[Blurite bolts (unf)|unfinished blurite bolts]]. This requires a [[Smithing]] level of 8, and for each [[blurite bar]] that player smiths they will get 10 unfinished blurite bolts and 17 Smithing [[experience]]. Then a player must attach flights to the bolts. Attaching flights to each bolt requires a [[Fletching]] level of 24 and 1 [[feather]], granting 1 Fletching experience per bolt.
Blurite bolts may be tipped with [[Jade (gem)|jade]]. A player must first have a Fletching level of 26 and take a cut jade and use a chisel with it to make 12 [[jade bolt tips]], granting 2 Fletching experience. Attaching jade bolt tips also requires a Fletching level of 26, and for each jade bolt tip attached to a blurite bolt, a player is granted 2.4 Fletching experience. Once the jade bolt tips have been attached, the blurite bolts become [[jade bolts]]. Jade bolts can then be enchanted to become [[jade bolts (e)]].
