{{External|rsc=Faladian Knight's sword|rs}} {{Infobox Item |name = Blurite sword |image = [[File:Blurite sword.png]] |release = [[6 April]] [[2001]] |update = Massive update! |members = No |quest = [[The Knight's Sword]] |tradeable = No |equipable = Yes |stackable = No |noteable = No |options = Wield, Drop |examine = A Faladian Knight's sword. |value = 200 |weight = 1.814 |id = 667 }} [[File:Blurite sword detail.png|left|100px]] The '''blurite sword''' is a longsword [[quest items|quest item]] used only in [[The Knight's Sword]]. It requires 1 [[Attack]] to wield, and is obtained by giving a [[blurite ore]] and two [[iron bar]]s to [[Thurgo]] after showing him a portrait of the sword.
The blurite sword has the same attack and defence bonuses as a [[steel longsword]] with the strength bonus of an [[iron longsword]]. It is slightly worse than [[Silverlight]]. Because of this and the fact that there is no Attack level needed to wield it, the blurite sword is sought by some lower level players at the start of the game.
Duplicates of the sword can be obtained by bringing Thurgo an extra blurite ore and two iron bars. During the quest, any swords must be [[drop trick]]ed to obtain duplicates, but this is not necessary after quest completion.
