{{Infobox Scenery |version1 = Teak |version2 = Mahogany |version3 = Marble |version4 = Raging Echoes |name = Boat Portal |image1 = [[File:Boat Portal (teak).png|250x250px]] |image2 = [[File:Boat Portal (mahogany).png|250x250px]] |image3 = [[File:Boat Portal (marble).png|250x250px]] |image4 = [[File:Boat Portal (Raging Echoes).png|250x250px]] |release = [[25 February]] [[2026]] |update = Cow Boss is Out Today! |members = Yes |location = [[Portal Chamber]] |options = Enter, Remove |examine = A gateway to your boat's last mooring point. |map = No |id1 = 60799 |id2 = 60809 |id3 = 60819 |id4 = 60783 }} A '''Boat Portal''' can be built in the [[portal chamber]] of a [[player-owned house]]. It will teleport players to the [[File:Docking_point_icon.png]] [[mooring point]] where their [[boat|player-owned boat]] is currently located. It requires the user's boat to have a [[Greater_teleport_focus_(facility)|greater teleport focus]] on it.
Players must first build a portal frame, then use the centrepiece to direct the portal. This requires level 67 [[Magic]] and completion of [[Pandemonium]]. The cost to direct the portal is 200 [[earth rune]]s, 200 [[water rune]]s and 200 [[law rune]]s.
==Comparison== Portals use 100 times the runes of the base spell, whereas individual additions to the [[portal nexus]] use 1,000 times the amount. {| class="wikitable defaultcenter" !colspan=2| Teleport ! !colspan=2| Portal chamber ! !colspan=2| Portal nexus |- |{{plinkt|Earth rune}} x 2 ! |{{plinkt|Earth rune}} x 200 ! |{{plinkt|Earth rune}} x 2,000 |- |{{plinkt|Water rune}} x 2 ! |{{plinkt|Water rune}} x 200 ! |{{plinkt|Water rune}} x 2,000 |- |{{plinkt|Law rune}} x 2 ! |{{plinkt|Law rune}} x 200 ! |{{plinkt|Law rune}} x 2,000 |}
