{{External|rs}} {{Infobox Music |name = Body Parts |number = 267 |file = [[File:Body Parts.ogg]] |release = [[31 January]] [[2005]] |update = Creature of Fenkenstrain |members = Yes |location = [[Experiment Cave]] |hint = This track unlocks in Fenkenstrain's Dungeon. |quest = [[Creature of Fenkenstrain]] |instruments = Marimba, Tubular Bells, Church Organ, Orchestral Harp, Choir Aahs, Synth Brass 1, Tenor Sax, Baritone Sax, Pad 2 (warm), Reverse Cymbal, Percussion |duration = 04:40 |signature = 4/4 |composer = Ian Taylor |album = ''[[RuneScape-_Old School Combat Classics|RuneScape: Old School Combat Classics]]'' |map = {{Map|3456,9920|3456,9984|3584,9984|3584,9920|plane=0|mapID=-1|mtype=polygon|bucket=yes}} |cacheid = 342 |sortname = Body Parts |unlockdetail = Unlocked in the [[experiment cave]]. }} '''Body Parts''' is a [[music]] track that is unlocked in the [[experiment cave]].
==Analysis== It seems to start with a drum kit playing a syncopated line, then a Baritone Saxophone or Trombone plays a basic jazz rhythm on the drum beat. Later an organ begins to play and plays the chromatic runs more typical of RuneScape Music tracks, while a Marimba plays a background countermelody, with the Baritone Sax or Trombone continuing to play the bass line much more softly.
==Versions== {| class="wikitable embed-audio-links" |- !Version !Release !Music Track |- |1 |17 – 24 November 2004 |[[File:Body Parts (v1).ogg]] |- |2 |[[6 March]] [[2007]] |[[File:Body Parts.ogg]] |}
{{Creature of Fenkenstrain}} {{Music}}

{{Infobox Item |name = Body core |image = [[File:Body core.png]] |release = [[14 April]] [[2021]] |update = Below Ice Mountain |members = No |quest = No |tradeable = No |equipable = No |stackable = No |noteable = No |options = Drop |examine = The corrupted core of a Body Golem. |value = 14 |weight = 0.020 |id = 25698 }} [[File:Body core detail.png|left|130px]] '''Body cores''' are the corrupted cores of [[Body Golem]]s, imbued with the power of the [[Body Altar]]. They can be used in place of [[rune essence|rune]] or [[pure essence]], but only for crafting body runes. Each core gives 75 [[Runecraft]] experience and 11 [[body rune]]s.
Like regular essence, the amount of body runes crafted will increase with the player's Runecraft level; for example, each body core will craft 33 body runes at level 92 Runecraft.
Golem cores cannot be placed in [[essence pouch]]es. If players attempt to store them in one, a chatbox message will appear, stating "''The golem core is too big to fit in an essence pouch.''"
The [[Charm of Luck]] buff purchasable from [[Ramarno's Shard Exchange]] does affect the drop chance of the core.
