==Standard dialogue==
===First time===
* '''Biles:''' Oh, hello there. Welcome to the Drumstick Kingdom. King Biles is the name. I am the ruler of this land.
* '''Player:''' You are?
* '''Biles:''' That's right. Once I was a banknote exchange merchant, but after becoming stranded here, I decided to make the best of it.
* '''Player:''' Okay...
* {{tselect|Select an option}}
* {{topt|Can you exchange some banknotes for me?}}
** '''Player:''' Can you exchange some banknotes for me?
** '''Biles:''' Well, it's not something I do as much now that I'm a king, but I suppose I can. Just hand me the banknotes you wish me to exchange. It will cost you 5 coins for each banknote.
** {{tact|end}}
* {{topt|The Drumstick Kingdom?}}
** '''Player:''' The Drumstick Kingdom?
** '''Biles:''' Yes, I wanted to call this place Drumstick Isle because I thought it looked like a chicken drumstick, but apparently that name was taken. I settled for Drumstick Kingdom instead.
** '''Player:''' So that's the name of this island?
** '''Biles:''' No, just the kingdom. This island already had a name as well, so I can't change it. It all seems stupid to me. It's not like there's some central authority in charge of naming islands!
** '''Biles:''' Besides, I'm a king! I should get to name whatever I want, just like Sleve does. He gets to name everything. He even named me! Before all this, my name was Friedrich Henglebert!
** '''Player:''' Right... Well, good luck with... the kingdom.
** {{tact|end}}
* {{topt|I need to get going.}}
** '''Player:''' I need to get going.
** '''Biles:''' Very well.
** {{tact|end}}

===Subsequent times===
* '''Biles:''' Oh, hello again. Welcome back to the Drumstick Kingdom.
* {{tact|above}}

