{{Transcript|scenery}} ==Core== ===Hull=== {| class="wikitable sortable align-center-1" !Component !Sloop/Skiff !Component !Raft |- |Wooden hull||A sturdy hull made from wooden hull parts.||Wooden base||A base for a raft made from logs. |- |Oak hull||A sturdy hull made from oak hull parts.||Oak base||A base for a raft made from oak logs. |- |Teak hull||A sturdy hull made from teak hull parts.||Teak base||A base for a raft made from teak logs. |- |Mahogany hull||A sturdy hull made from mahogany hull parts.||Mahogany base||A base for a raft made from mahogany logs. |- |Camphor hull||A sturdy hull made from camphor hull parts.||Camphor base||A base for a raft made from camphor logs. |- |Ironwood hull||A sturdy hull made from ironwood hull parts.||Ironwood base||A base for a raft made from ironwood logs. |- |Rosewood hull||A sturdy hull made from rosewood hull parts.||Rosewood base||A base for a raft made from rosewood logs. |}
===Keel=== {| class="wikitable sortable align-center-1" !Component !Sloop/Skiff |- |Bronze keel||A durable keel made from bronze keel parts. |- |Iron keel||A durable keel made from iron keel parts. |- |Steel keel||A durable keel made from steel keel parts. |- |Mithril keel||A durable keel made from mithril keel parts. |- |Adamant keel||A durable keel made from adamant keel parts. |- |Rune keel||A durable keel made from rune keel parts. |- |Dragon keel||A durable keel made from dragon keel parts. |} ===Helm=== {| class="wikitable sortable align-center-1" !Component !Sloop/Skiff/Raft |- |Bronze helm||A strong helm made of bronze and wood. |- |Iron helm||A strong helm made of iron and oak. |- |Steel helm||A strong helm made of steel and teak. |- |Mithril helm||A strong helm made of mithril and mahogany. |- |Adamant helm||A strong helm made of adamant and camphor. |- |Rune helm||A strong helm made of rune and ironwood. |- |Dragon helm||A strong helm made of dragon and rosewood. |} ===Sails=== {| class="wikitable sortable align-center-1" !Component !Sloop/Skiff/Raft |- |Wooden mast and linen s...||A wooden mast flying sails made of linen. |- |Oak mast and linen sails||An oak mast flying sails made of linen. |- |Teak mast and canvas sails||A teak mast flying sails made of canvas. |- |Mahogany mast and canva...||A mahogany mast flying sails made of canvas. |- |Camphor mast and canvas...||A camphor mast flying sails made of canvas. |- |Ironwood mast and cotto...||An ironwood mast flying sails made of cotton. |- |Rosewood mast and cotto...||A rosewood mast flying sails made of cotton. |} ===Trim=== {| class="wikitable sortable align-center-1" !Component !Sloop/Skiff |- |No trim||Your boat without any painted trims. |- |Angler's trim||A salmon pink trim to decorate your boat. Doesn't smell as fishy as you'd expect. |- |Armadylean trim||A bright white trim to decorate your boat in the colour of Armadyl. So far not known to attract aviansies. |- |Barracuda trim||A light blue trim to decorate your boat Barracuda style! |- |Guthixian trim||A balanced green trim to decorate your boat in the colour of Guthix. Makes the planks feel like trees again. |- |Inky trim||An inky black trim to decorate your boat. Does not increase your stealth. |- |Merchant's trim||A shiny golden trim to decorate your boat. While gold can't buy you happiness, it certainly can buy you style. |- |Salvor's trim||An aquamarine trim to decorate your boat. Not to be confused with adamant. |- |Saradominist trim||A strong blue trim to decorate your boat in the colour of Saradomin. Does not make surrounding water holy. |- |Sandy trim||A sandy beige trim to decorate your boat. Is not coarse, rough or irritating. Does not get everywhere. |- |Shark trim||A sharp grey trim to decorate your boat. Makes you one with the sharks. |- |Zamorakian trim||A powerful red trim to decorate your boat in the colour of Zamorak. Does not make you faster, but possibly more chaotic. |} ===Flag=== {| class="wikitable sortable align-center-1" !Component !Sloop/Skiff/Raft |- |Storm chaser's flag||A flag awarded to those who have achieved Marlin rank at the Tempor Tantrum Barracuda Trial. |- |Swamp cruiser's flag||A flag awarded to those who have achieved Marlin rank at the Jubbly Jive Barracuda Trial. |- |Crystal glider's flag||A flag awarded to those who have achieved Marlin rank at the Gwenith Glide Barracuda Trial. |} ===Brazier=== {| class="wikitable sortable align-center-1" !Component !Sloop/Skiff/Raft |- |Eternal brazier||An ever burning flame to stave off all but the coldest of conditions at sea. |} ==Facilities== ===Salvaging=== {| class="wikitable sortable align-center-1" !Facility !Sloop/Skiff/Raft |- |Bronze salvaging hook||A salvaging hook made from bronze and wood. |- |Iron salvaging hook||A salvaging hook made from iron and oak. |- |Steel salvaging hook||A salvaging hook made from steel and teak. |- |Mithril salvaging hook||A salvaging hook made from mithril and mahogany. |- |Adamant salvaging hook||A salvaging hook made from adamant and camphor. |- |Rune salvaging hook||A salvaging hook made from rune and ironwood. |- |Dragon salvaging hook||A salvaging hook made from dragon and rosewood. |} ===Trawling=== {| class="wikitable sortable align-center-1" !Facility !Sloop/Skiff |- |Hemp trawling net||A trawling net woven from hemp. |- |Rope trawling net||A trawling net woven from rope. |- |Linen trawling net||A trawling net woven from linen. |- |Cotton trawling net||A trawling net woven from hemp. |- |Fathom stone||A stone capable of peering into the depths of the ocean. Useful for detecting the rough locations of nearby shoals at sea. |- |Fathom pearl||A fathom stone enhanced by a rare pearl found in the ocean. Can pinpoint the exact location of fish shoals. |} ===Storage=== {| class="wikitable sortable align-center-1" !Facility !Sloop !Skiff !Raft |- |Cargo hold||A wooden cargo hold for larger vessels.||A wooden cargo hold for smaller vessels.||A wooden cargo hold for an especially small vessel. |- |Oak cargo hold||An oak cargo hold for larger vessels.||A oak cargo hold for smaller vessels.||A oak cargo hold for an especially small vessel. |- |Teak cargo hold||A teak cargo hold for larger vessels.||A teak cargo hold for smaller vessels.||A teak cargo hold for an especially small vessel. |- |Mahogany cargo hold||A mahogany cargo hold for larger vessels.||A mahogany cargo hold for smaller vessels.||A mahogany cargo hold for an especially small vessel. |- |Camphor cargo hold||A camphor cargo hold for larger vessels.||A camphor cargo hold for smaller vessels.||A camphor cargo hold for an especially small vessel. |- |Ironwood cargo hold||An ironwood cargo hold for larger vessels.||A ironwood cargo hold for smaller vessels.||A ironwood cargo hold for an especially small vessel. |- |Rosewood cargo hold||A rosewood cargo hold for larger vessels.||A rosewood cargo hold for smaller vessels.||A rosewood cargo hold for an especially small vessel. |} ===Stations=== {| class="wikitable sortable align-center-1" !Facility !Sloop/Skiff |- |Inoculation station||A disease neutralising station for countering fetid waters. |- |Salvaging station||A station to sort through salvage collected at sea. |- |Chum station||A station that can be used to spread basic fish offcuts into the sea while deep sea trawling. |- |Advanced chum station||A station that can be used to spread all types of fish offcuts into the sea while deep sea trawling. |- |Chum spreader||A station that can be used to spread all types of fish offcuts into the sea while deep sea trawling. When doing so, it can take offcuts directly from the cargo hold. |} ===Wind=== {| class="wikitable sortable align-center-1" !Facility !Sloop/Skiff !Raft |- |Wind catcher|| colspan="2" |Used for catching and storing wind motes. Once caught, wind motes can be released into your sails for a speed boost. |- |Crystal extractor||Periodically generates wind motes for a wind catching facility.||Unavailable |- |Gale catcher|| colspan="2" |Used for catching and storing wind motes. Once caught, wind motes can be released into your sails for a speed boost. |}
===Misc=== {| class="wikitable sortable align-center-1" !Facility !Sloop !Skiff !Raft |- |Range|| colspan="3" |A range to cook all sorts of cuisine. Your kitchen away from home. |- |Keg|| colspan="3" |A keg to store various brews that can buff you and your crew's actions on your boat. |- |Anchor||An anchor fit for larger vessels.||An anchor fit for smaller vessels.||Unavailable |- |Teleport focus|| colspan="3" |Allows you to teleport the boat to the dock or mooring point you are at. |- |Greater teleport focus|| colspan="3" |Allows you to both teleport the boat to the dock or mooring point you are at as well as letting you teleport to where the boat is docked. |} ===Cannons=== {| class="wikitable sortable align-center-1" !Facility !Sloop/Skiff/Raft |- |Bronze cannon||A cannon made from bronze and wood. |- |Iron cannon||A cannon made from iron and oak. |- |Steel cannon||A cannon made from steel and teak. |- |Mithril cannon||A cannon made from mithril and mahogany. |- |Adamant cannon||A cannon made from adamant and camphor. |- |Rune cannon||A cannon made from rune and ironwood. |- |Dragon cannon||A cannon made from dragon and rosewood. |}

